    <node id="Red Blood Cells">
      <data key="d0">Red Blood Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Red Blood Cells are responsible for carrying oxygen throughout the body and play a critical role in cellular respiration. They are also known as red blood cells (RBCs) or erythrocytes. Red blood cells are essential for transporting nutrients and removing waste from tissues. These cells are produced in the bone marrow and are measured in a complete blood count to assess overall health. Red blood cells are a type of blood cell that carries oxygen throughout the body, and their levels may be low in patients with conditions such as chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL). The primary function of red blood cells is to deliver oxygen to cells and tissues, ensuring proper metabolic function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
