    <node id="HER2-Targeted Therapy">
      <data key="d0">HER2-Targeted Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">HER2-targeted therapy is a treatment that specifically targets HER2-positive breast cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;HER2-targeted therapy is a type of systemic treatment that specifically targets HER2-positive cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;HER2-targeted therapy is a treatment method that specifically targets HER2 proteins.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839627</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Plasma">
      <data key="d0">Plasma</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Plasma is the liquid component of blood, primarily composed of water and dissolved substances. It serves as the fluid medium that transports various elements throughout the body. Plasma is described as a clear, yellowish fluid that carries blood cells, nutrients, and other essential substances. It functions as the primary vehicle for transporting these materials, playing a critical role in maintaining bodily functions. The descriptions consistently highlight its composition, emphasizing its high water content and its role in carrying cells and nutrients. Plasma acts as the liquid component of blood, responsible for distributing vital substances across the circulatory system. All descriptions agree on its fundamental role in supporting the movement of cells, nutrients, and other dissolved materials within the bloodstream.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839627</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Endocrine Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Endocrine Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Endocrine Therapy is a treatment that blocks estrogen receptor signaling in breast cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Endocrine therapy is a treatment that targets hormone receptors in cancer cells to slow or stop their growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Endocrine therapy is a systemic treatment that blocks hormones from reaching cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Endocrine therapy refers to medical treatment that affects the endocrine system, often used in managing hormonal conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Endocrine therapy is a treatment method that targets hormone receptors in cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Endocrine therapy is a treatment that blocks estrogen or progesterone to treat hormone receptor-positive breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839627</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Platelets">
      <data key="d0">Platelets</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Platelets are small cell fragments in the blood that help control bleeding and form clots. They play a critical role in the process of hemostasis, where they aggregate at the site of injuries to stop bleeding. Platelets are also referred to as thrombocytes or PLTs and are essential for maintaining proper blood clotting function. These cell fragments are involved in both clot formation and wound healing, contributing to the body's ability to repair damaged tissues. Platelets are not fully developed cells but rather cytoplasmic fragments derived from megakaryocytes in the bone marrow. In addition to their role in clotting, platelets are measured in a complete blood count (CBC) to assess their quantity and functionality. Abnormal platelet levels can indicate various health conditions, such as thrombocytopenia (low platelet count) or thrombocytosis (high platelet count), and may be associated with diseases like chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL). Overall, platelets are vital components of the circulatory system, ensuring effective response to vascular injuries and maintaining hemostatic balance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-81c87ec3c2682da4d531da53f6e5e18c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839627</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Breast Reconstruction">
      <data key="d0">Breast Reconstruction</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Breast reconstruction is a surgical procedure to rebuild the breast after a mastectomy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
