    <node id="Local Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Local Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Local therapy focuses on treating cancer in specific areas such as the breast, chest wall, and lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839628</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Clinical Trial">
      <data key="d0">Clinical Trial</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Clinical Trial is a research study designed to evaluate new treatments, therapies, or interventions for medical conditions, including cancer and other diseases. These studies often involve human participants and aim to assess the safety, effectiveness, and potential benefits of new approaches such as chemotherapy, targeted therapy, immunotherapy, and novel drugs. Clinical trials may focus on specific types of cancer, such as bladder cancer, gliomas, lung cancer, and leukemia, and are sometimes recommended for patients with recurrent or advanced disease. They may also explore treatments for rare cancers or conditions like primary CNS lymphoma and metastatic thyroid cancer. In addition to treatment evaluation, some clinical trials focus on prevention strategies or diagnostic methods. Patients participating in clinical trials may have access to new treatment options that are not yet widely available. These studies are essential for advancing medical knowledge and improving patient care. Clinical trials can involve testing new medications, devices, or procedures and are conducted under strict scientific and ethical guidelines. They may be considered for patients based on eligibility criteria, such as performance status, and are often organized by academic institutions, pharmaceutical companies, or government agencies. Overall, clinical trials play a critical role in the development and validation of new medical interventions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
