    </node>
    <node id="PARP Inhibitor">
      <data key="d0">PARP Inhibitor</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">PARP inhibitors are a class of drugs used in the treatment of ovarian cancer, particularly in maintenance therapy after initial treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A PARP inhibitor is a drug that targets the PARP enzyme, which is involved in DNA repair in cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839630</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chemotherapy Examples">
      <data key="d0">Chemotherapy Examples</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Chemotherapy examples include drugs such as Capecitabine, Carboplatin, Cisplatin, Cyclophosphamide, Docetaxel, Doxorubicin, Epirubicin, Eribulin, Fluorouracil, Methotrexate, Paclitaxel, and Vinorelbine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839630</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sentinel Lymph Node Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Sentinel Lymph Node Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Sentinel Lymph Node Biopsy is a medical procedure used to determine whether cancer has spread to the lymph nodes. The procedure involves identifying and removing the sentinel lymph nodes, which are the first nodes that cancer is likely to reach from the primary tumor site. Sentinel Lymph Node Biopsy (SLNB) is specifically designed to check for the presence of cancer cells in these nodes, providing critical information about the extent of cancer progression. During the procedure, tissue samples are removed from the sentinel lymph nodes to be analyzed in a laboratory. This technique is widely used in cancer diagnosis, particularly in cases such as breast cancer, to guide treatment decisions and assess the need for further interventions. The goal of the procedure is to accurately detect whether cancer has spread beyond the original site, allowing for more targeted and effective treatment strategies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839630</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inhibitor Examples">
      <data key="d0">Inhibitor Examples</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Inhibitor examples include Abemaciclib, Alpelisib, Everolimus, Olaparib, Palbociclib, Ribociclib, and Talazoparib.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839631</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Immunotherapy Example">
      <data key="d0">Immunotherapy Example</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">An immunotherapy example is Pembrolizumab, which is used to treat certain types of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839631</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="HER2-Targeted Therapy Examples">
      <data key="d0">HER2-Targeted Therapy Examples</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">HER2-targeted therapy examples include Pertuzumab, Trastuzumab, Ado-trastuzumab emtansine, Fam-trastuzumab deruxtecan-nxki, Lapatinib, Margetuximab-cmkb, Neratinib, Tucatinib, and Phesgo.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839631</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mastectomy Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Mastectomy Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Mastectomy surgery is a procedure to remove all or part of the breast, often used in the treatment of inflammatory breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839631</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Modified Radical Mastectomy">
      <data key="d0">Modified Radical Mastectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">A modified radical mastectomy is a type of mastectomy that removes the breast and underarm lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Modified radical mastectomy is a surgical procedure involving the removal of the entire breast and some lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839631</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radiation Therapy Sessions">
      <data key="d0">Radiation Therapy Sessions</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Radiation therapy sessions are short treatments given daily over a few days to weeks to kill cancer cells and shrink tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839631</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="General Anesthesia">
      <data key="d0">General Anesthesia</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">General anesthesia is a state of controlled unconsciousness used during surgical procedures to ensure the patient does not feel pain.&lt;SEP&gt;General anesthesia is a medical technique that puts a patient into a deep sleep to prevent pain during surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839631</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Care Team">
      <data key="d0">Care Team</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Care Team is a group of healthcare professionals who work together to provide comprehensive care and support to patients. It consists of medical professionals who collaborate to manage a patient's treatment, recovery, and overall well-being. The Care Team is responsible for diagnosing and treating a patient's condition, offering guidance, and ensuring coordinated care throughout the medical process. This team typically includes various specialists who work in unison to address the unique needs of each individual. In some descriptions, the Care Team is specifically noted as being involved in cancer treatment, including cases such as AML and pancreatic cancer, where they play a critical role in evaluating patients, asking about symptoms, and providing treatment guidance. The Care Team is also described as a multidisciplinary group focused on delivering both medical treatment and emotional or practical support. Overall, the Care Team functions as a unified unit aimed at improving patient outcomes through collaborative and comprehensive healthcare delivery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839632</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Systemic Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Systemic Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Systemic Therapy is a cancer treatment approach that involves the administration of drugs or other agents that travel through the bloodstream to affect cells throughout the body. It is designed to target cancer cells that may have spread beyond their original location, making it particularly useful for advanced or metastatic cancers. Systemic therapy encompasses a range of treatments, including chemotherapy, targeted therapy, immunotherapy, and in some cases, endocrine therapy. These treatments work systemically, meaning they impact the entire body rather than just a localized area. 

The therapy is often used when cancer has progressed beyond the skin or other initial sites, and it may be employed in various stages of treatment, such as before surgery to shrink tumors or after local therapies like radiation or surgery. It can also be used in conjunction with other treatments to manage the disease. While systemic therapy is effective in targeting cancer cells throughout the body, it can also affect normal cells, leading to potential side effects. 

Systemic Therapy is commonly applied in the management of different types of cancer, including basal cell skin cancer, cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma (CSCC), acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL), cervical cancer, and thyroid cancer, among others. The specific type of systemic therapy used depends on the cancer type, stage, and patient condition. It is typically administered intravenously, though other routes may be used depending on the treatment. Overall, systemic therapy plays a critical role in treating cancers that have spread and offers a comprehensive approach to managing malignant diseases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839632</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radioactive Substance">
      <data key="d0">Radioactive Substance</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A radioactive substance is injected into the skin near a tumor to help locate sentinel lymph nodes during a biopsy.&lt;SEP&gt;A radioactive substance is used in PET scans to highlight cancerous cells in the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839632</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blue-Colored Substance">
      <data key="d0">Blue-Colored Substance</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A blue-colored substance is used in conjunction with a radioactive substance to identify sentinel lymph nodes during surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839632</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Clinical Trials">
      <data key="d0">Clinical Trials</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Clinical Trials are research studies designed to test new treatments, drugs, procedures, or devices in human participants to evaluate their safety and effectiveness. These studies aim to advance medical knowledge and improve treatment outcomes for various conditions, particularly cancer. Clinical trials often focus on specific types of cancer, such as squamous cell skin cancer, ovarian cancer, pancreatic cancer, cervical cancer, and thyroid cancer, among others. They may also explore new ways of fighting cancer or improving patient care. Participants in clinical trials are typically informed about the study's purpose and risks, and their involvement is essential for the development of new therapies. Clinical trials play a critical role in the medical field by providing evidence-based data that can lead to better treatments and potentially life-saving innovations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839632</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wound Healing">
      <data key="d0">Wound Healing</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Wound healing refers to the process by which the body repairs damaged skin after surgery, which can occur through different methods such as secondary intention or linear closure.&lt;SEP&gt;Wound healing is the process by which the body repairs damaged tissue, which can be affected by smoking and vaping.&lt;SEP&gt;Wound healing is the process by which the body repairs damaged tissue after an injury or surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839632</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Secondary Intention Healing">
      <data key="d0">Secondary Intention Healing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Secondary intention healing is a wound healing process where the wound is left open to heal naturally without stitches.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839633</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Linear Closure">
      <data key="d0">Linear Closure</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Linear closure is a wound healing technique where the surgeon reshapes the wound and stitches it in a line.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839633</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin Graft">
      <data key="d0">Skin Graft</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A skin graft is a patch of skin transplanted from one area of the body to another to aid in wound healing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839633</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Electrons">
      <data key="d0">Electrons</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Electrons are subatomic particles used in radiation therapy to treat superficial tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839633</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer is a group of diseases characterized by the uncontrolled growth and spread of abnormal cells. It is a disease that can affect various parts of the body and may require treatment that impacts fertility. Cancer is defined by the uncontrolled growth of abnormal cells, which can invade and damage surrounding tissues, and can spread to other parts of the body. This uncontrolled cell growth can lead to potential harm to the body and may cause strong emotional reactions and distress in patients. Cancer can be detected through imaging and biopsies, and treatments often include surgery, radiation therapy, and other interventions. Some descriptions mention that cancer can make quitting smoking more difficult, highlighting its complex relationship with lifestyle factors. Colon cancer is one specific type of cancer that originates in the colon. Overall, cancer is a broad category of diseases with varying forms and impacts, all sharing the common characteristic of uncontrolled cell growth and the potential to spread throughout the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839633</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymph Node">
      <data key="d0">Lymph Node</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymph Node is a small structure in the body that is part of the lymphatic system and plays a critical role in the immune system. These structures filter lymph, a clear fluid containing white blood cells, and help remove harmful substances such as bacteria and cancer cells. Lymph nodes are often examined for signs of cancer spread, as they can become affected by metastasis, where cancer cells from a primary tumor travel through the lymphatic system and settle in these nodes. In some cases, lymph nodes may contain cancer and are examined or removed during medical treatment. They serve as important sites for immune responses and are integral to the body's defense mechanisms. Lymph nodes are frequently involved in the progression of cancer, making their evaluation crucial in diagnosis and treatment planning. Their function in filtering lymph and supporting immune activity highlights their significance in maintaining overall health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839634</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Photons">
      <data key="d0">Photons</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Photons are high-energy particles used in radiation therapy to treat deeper, more invasive tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839634</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Protons">
      <data key="d0">Protons</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Protons are charged particles used in radiation therapy to target cancer cells with precision.&lt;SEP&gt;Protons are a form of high-energy radiation used in radiation therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839634</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pathologist">
      <data key="d0">Pathologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Pathologist is a medical doctor who examines tissues, cells, and bodily fluids to diagnose diseases, including various types of cancer. Pathologists play a critical role in identifying the presence, type, and characteristics of diseases by analyzing samples obtained through biopsies, surgeries, or other medical procedures. They use microscopes to study tissue and cell samples, looking for abnormal changes that may indicate illness. In the context of cancer, pathologists determine whether a tumor is malignant or benign, identify the specific type of cancer, and assess its grade or severity. Their findings are essential for guiding treatment decisions and patient care. Pathologists also analyze fluid samples and organs removed during surgical procedures to detect and diagnose a wide range of diseases beyond cancer. As specialists in pathology, they contribute significantly to both diagnostic and research efforts in medicine. The work of a pathologist involves a high level of expertise and precision, as their conclusions directly impact clinical outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839634</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Surgery is a medical procedure used to remove tumors, cancerous tissue, or affected organs, often as a primary treatment for various types of cancer. It involves the excision of cancerous lesions and surrounding tissues to prevent further spread and improve patient outcomes. Surgery is commonly employed in the treatment of basal cell skin cancer, squamous cell skin cancer, breast cancer, ovarian cancer, pancreatic cancer, prostate cancer, cervical cancer, and thyroid cancer. In some cases, such as early-stage cervical cancer, it may involve the removal of the cervix or uterus, while in others, like prostate cancer, it may include the removal of the entire prostate gland. For certain cancers, such as non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) and colon cancer, surgery is used to remove cancerous tissue from the body, sometimes along with nearby lymph nodes. Surgery is also a treatment option for gliomas, where the goal is to remove as much of the tumor as possible, especially for Grade 1 gliomas. In addition, it is used for bone tumors and bladder cancer, with the extent of the procedure depending on the stage and location of the disease. However, surgery is not always recommended, particularly for conditions like primary central nervous system (CNS) lymphoma, due to the risks associated with brain surgery. Overall, surgery remains a critical intervention in oncology, though its feasibility and approach vary based on the type, stage, and location of the cancer, as well as the patient’s overall health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
