      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Basal Cell Nevus Syndrome">
      <data key="d0">Basal Cell Nevus Syndrome</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Basal cell nevus syndrome is a genetic condition that increases the risk of skin cancer when exposed to radiation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839634</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Xeroderma Pigmentosum">
      <data key="d0">Xeroderma Pigmentosum</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Xeroderma pigmentosum (XP) is a genetic syndrome that impairs the body's ability to repair DNA damage from sunlight, increasing the risk of skin cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Xeroderma pigmentosum is a genetic condition that increases the risk of skin cancer when exposed to radiation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839635</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lupus">
      <data key="d0">Lupus</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lupus is a connective tissue disease that may make radiation therapy less appropriate for some patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Lupus is an autoimmune disease in which the immune system attacks healthy tissues and organs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839635</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Scleroderma">
      <data key="d0">Scleroderma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Scleroderma is a connective tissue disease that may make radiation therapy less appropriate for some patients.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839635</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adjuvant Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Adjuvant Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Adjuvant therapy is treatment given after primary cancer treatment to reduce the risk of cancer recurrence.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjuvant therapy is chemotherapy given after surgery to reduce cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839635</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin Redness">
      <data key="d0">Skin Redness</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Skin redness is a common short-term side effect of radiation therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839635</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Itching">
      <data key="d0">Itching</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Itching is a common short-term side effect of radiation therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839636</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="External Beam Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d0">External Beam Radiation Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">External Beam Radiation Therapy (EBRT) is a type of radiation therapy that delivers radiation from outside the body to the tumor site. It is a treatment method that uses external machines to deliver radiation, targeting cancer cells with high-energy rays or waves. EBRT is a form of radiation therapy that delivers radiation from outside the body, and it is also described as a treatment method that uses high-energy radiation to target and destroy cancer cells. The therapy is specifically used in the treatment of cancer, including cases involving the bladder, where it targets and kills cancer cells. EBRT is often referred to as a type of radiation treatment that focuses on cancer cells from outside the body, utilizing high-energy waves or rays to achieve its therapeutic effect. The term EBRT stands for External Beam Radiation Therapy, and it is consistently characterized as a method of delivering radiation externally to treat various types of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839636</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radiation Oncologist">
      <data key="d0">Radiation Oncologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Radiation Oncologist is a medical professional who specializes in the use of radiation therapy to treat cancer. Radiation Oncologists are doctors who use radiation therapy as a primary treatment method for various types of cancer, including thyroid cancer and anal cancer. They are responsible for prescribing and delivering radiation therapy, as well as planning and overseeing the treatment process. A radiation oncologist is a physician who utilizes radiation therapy to treat cancer, and they play a critical role in developing individualized treatment plans for patients. These specialists are trained to administer radiation in a precise and controlled manner to target cancerous cells while minimizing damage to healthy tissue. Radiation Oncologists are also referred to as medical professionals who use radiation therapy to treat cancer, and they work closely with other healthcare providers to ensure comprehensive patient care. Their expertise includes not only the technical aspects of radiation delivery but also the clinical judgment required to determine the most effective treatment strategies for different cancers. Overall, Radiation Oncologists are essential members of the cancer treatment team, providing specialized care through the use of radiation therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839636</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Brachytherapy">
      <data key="d0">Brachytherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Brachytherapy is a form of radiation therapy where radioactive material or sources are placed inside or near the tumor. This method involves positioning the radiation source close to the cancerous tissue, either within the body or directly at the tumor site. Brachytherapy is often used in conjunction with external beam radiation therapy to enhance treatment effectiveness. The technique allows for targeted delivery of radiation, minimizing exposure to surrounding healthy tissues. Different descriptions emphasize variations in placement, such as inside the body, near the tumor, or directly into the affected area. Overall, brachytherapy is classified as a type of radiation therapy that delivers localized radiation treatment. The core principle remains consistent across descriptions: the use of radioactive materials placed in proximity to the tumor for therapeutic purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839636</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mild Discomfort">
      <data key="d0">Mild Discomfort</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mild discomfort is a common short-term side effect of radiation therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
