    <node id="Cisplatin">
      <data key="d0">Cisplatin</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Cisplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in the treatment of various cancers. It is specifically noted for its application in treating squamous cell skin cancer, ovarian cancer, cervical cancer, bladder cancer, and anal cancer. Cisplatin is often administered intravenously and is frequently used in combination with other drugs, such as 5-FU, for the treatment of anal cancer and perianal cancer. The drug is known for its effectiveness but also for potential side effects, including hypersensitivity reactions and kidney damage. As a platinum-based agent, Cisplatin works by interfering with DNA replication, thereby inhibiting cancer cell growth. It is commonly used in various chemotherapy regimens, particularly for metastatic cervical cancer and other advanced stages of cancer. Despite its therapeutic benefits, its use requires careful monitoring due to its toxicities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839636</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
