    <node id="PDEMA">
      <data key="d0">PDEMA</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">PDEMA is a type of surgery used to assess and remove cancerous tissue while preserving healthy tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;PDEMA is a medical procedure mentioned in the context of skin cancer treatment, often followed by a skin graft.&lt;SEP&gt;PDEMA stands for Peripheral Dermatologic Excision with Margin Assessment, a technique used in the treatment of skin cancers, often in conjunction with Mohs surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;PDEMA stands for Precision-Directed Excision and Margin Assessment, a surgical technique used in cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
