    <node id="Uterus">
      <data key="d0">Uterus</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The uterus is a female reproductive organ that can be examined during a pelvic exam.&lt;SEP&gt;The uterus is a hollow organ in the female reproductive system where a fetus develops during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;The uterus is an organ that may be affected by ovarian cancer, as seen in stage 2A.&lt;SEP&gt;The uterus is the organ where a baby develops during pregnancy and is part of the female reproductive system.&lt;SEP&gt;Uterus is a female reproductive organ where a fertilized egg implants and develops during pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Uterus is a female reproductive organ where a fertilized egg implants and develops.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839637</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cervix">
      <data key="d0">Cervix</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The cervix is the lower part of the uterus that is checked during a pelvic exam.&lt;SEP&gt;The cervix is the lower part of the uterus that connects to the vagina and plays a role in reproduction.&lt;SEP&gt;The cervix is the lower part of the uterus that connects to the vagina and is a key site for cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The cervix is the lower part of the uterus that connects to the vagina and is the focus of cervical cancer diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;The cervix is the lower part of the uterus that connects to the vagina.&lt;SEP&gt;Cervix is the lower part of the uterus that connects to the vagina.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839637</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vagina">
      <data key="d0">Vagina</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The vagina is a part of the female reproductive system that is examined during a pelvic exam.&lt;SEP&gt;The vagina is a muscular canal that connects the cervix to the outside of the body, serving as a passage for sexual intercourse and childbirth.&lt;SEP&gt;The vagina is the muscular passage through which a baby is born and is part of the female reproductive system.&lt;SEP&gt;Vagina is a muscular canal that connects the cervix to the outside of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Vagina is the muscular canal leading from the uterus to the outside of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Vagina is a muscular canal leading from the uterus to the outside of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839637</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carboplatin">
      <data key="d0">Carboplatin</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Carboplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in the treatment of various cancers, including squamous cell skin cancer, ovarian cancer, and cervical cancer. It is commonly administered in combination with other drugs such as paclitaxel for the treatment of ovarian cancer. Carboplatin is considered an alternative to cisplatin when the latter is not suitable, and it is similar in structure and function to cisplatin. While effective in treating several types of cancer, carboplatin has been associated with potential side effects, including hypersensitivity reactions. As a platinum-based agent, it works by interfering with DNA replication and cell division, thereby inhibiting the growth of cancer cells. The drug is widely used in oncology due to its broad applicability across different cancer types.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839638</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parametrium">
      <data key="d0">Parametrium</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The parametrium is the fat and connective tissue surrounding the uterus and cervix, connecting it to the pelvis.&lt;SEP&gt;Parametrium is the connective tissue surrounding the uterus, often examined for cancer spread.&lt;SEP&gt;The parametrium is the fat and connective tissue surrounding the cervix and uterus, involved in cervical cancer staging.&lt;SEP&gt;The Parametrium is the tissue surrounding the uterus and may be involved in advanced cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839638</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Small Cell Neuroendocrine Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Small Cell Neuroendocrine Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Small Cell Neuroendocrine Carcinoma (NECC) is a rare and aggressive type of cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839638</data>
