    <node id="Transvaginal Ultrasound">
      <data key="d0">Transvaginal Ultrasound</data>
      <data key="d1">equipment</data>
      <data key="d2">A transvaginal ultrasound involves inserting a probe into the vagina to get detailed images of the ovaries.&lt;SEP&gt;Transvaginal Ultrasound is a medical imaging technique using sound waves to examine the pelvic area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839638</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fertility-Sparing Treatment">
      <data key="d0">Fertility-Sparing Treatment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fertility-Sparing Treatment refers to medical approaches that aim to preserve a patient's ability to conceive after cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertility-sparing treatment is an option for early cervical cancer that preserves reproductive organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertility-Sparing Treatment is an approach that allows for future pregnancy by preserving the uterus and ovaries.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertility-sparing treatment refers to cancer treatments that aim to preserve a patient's ability to have children.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839638</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ovarian Transposition">
      <data key="d0">Ovarian Transposition</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Ovarian transposition is a surgical procedure that moves the ovaries out of the radiation field to protect them.&lt;SEP&gt;Ovarian Transposition is a surgical procedure that moves the ovaries out of the radiation field to protect them during cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Ovarian transposition is a surgery that moves the ovaries out of the radiation field to preserve fertility.&lt;SEP&gt;Ovarian transposition is a fertility preservation procedure that moves ovaries out of the radiation beam's path.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839639</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Oophoropexy">
      <data key="d0">Oophoropexy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Oophoropexy is the surgical procedure for ovarian transposition, where the ovaries are moved out of the radiation field.&lt;SEP&gt;Oophoropexy is a fertility preservation procedure that moves the ovaries out of the radiation beam's path.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839639</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Egg Freezing">
      <data key="d0">Egg Freezing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Egg freezing is a process of removing, freezing, and storing unfertilized eggs for future use in fertility treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;Egg freezing involves removing and freezing unfertilized eggs for later use in assisted reproduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Egg Freezing is a process where unfertilized eggs are extracted, frozen, and stored for future use.&lt;SEP&gt;Egg freezing is a fertility preservation method involving the freezing of unfertilized eggs for future use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839639</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radiotracer">
      <data key="d0">Radiotracer</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Radiotracer is a radioactive substance used in medical imaging to highlight areas of the body for diagnostic purposes. It is commonly employed in PET scans to track biological processes and identify areas of increased metabolic activity, particularly in the detection of cancer. Radiotracers are designed to release small amounts of radiation, allowing them to be safely used in various imaging tests, including bone scans that help detect cancer in the bones. These substances are integral to nuclear medicine, where they assist in visualizing internal body structures by accumulating in specific tissues or organs. The primary function of a radiotracer is to serve as a marker that enables doctors to observe physiological functions and identify abnormalities through advanced imaging techniques. Different types of radiotracers may be used depending on the specific imaging application and the area of the body being examined.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839639</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Surrogacy">
      <data key="d0">Surrogacy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Surrogacy is an arrangement where another person carries a pregnancy for someone else, often used in fertility treatments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839639</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CT Scan">
      <data key="d0">CT Scan</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">CT Scan is a medical imaging procedure that uses X-rays and computer technology to create detailed images of the body. It involves taking multiple X-ray images from different angles, which are then processed by a computer to generate cross-sectional or 3D images of internal structures. CT scans are widely used in diagnostic medicine for detecting a variety of conditions, including cancer, and are particularly valuable for identifying the spread of cancer to nearby lymph nodes or other areas of the body. The technique is also employed in monitoring cancer recurrence, assessing treatment response, and guiding biopsies. CT scans can be combined with other imaging methods such as PET scans in procedures like PET/CT. They are often used when alternative imaging methods, such as MRI, are not available or unsuitable. Additionally, CT scans play a role in pre-treatment planning, such as during simulation for radiation therapy, and are part of surveillance plans for certain cancers, including colon cancer. The procedure is non-invasive and provides detailed visual information that aids in diagnosis, staging, and ongoing patient management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
