    <node id="Staging">
      <data key="d0">Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Staging is a process used to describe the extent of cancer in the body, based on tumor size, lymph node involvement, and metastasis.&lt;SEP&gt;Staging is the process of determining the extent of cancer in the body to guide treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Staging is the process of determining how far cancer has spread in the body, based on imaging and other tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Staging is the process of determining the extent and spread of cancer in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Staging is a process used to determine the extent of cancer in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Staging is the process of determining how far cancer has spread in the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
