    <node id="Nicotine Withdrawal">
      <data key="d0">Nicotine Withdrawal</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nicotine withdrawal is the set of physical and psychological symptoms that occur when a person stops using nicotine-containing products.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicotine withdrawal refers to the physical and psychological symptoms experienced when quitting smoking or vaping.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicotine withdrawal refers to the physical and psychological challenges experienced when quitting smoking.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicotine withdrawal refers to the physical and psychological symptoms experienced when stopping tobacco use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Oropharynx">
      <data key="d0">Oropharynx</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The oropharynx is the part of the throat located behind the mouth, including the soft palate, tonsils, and base of the tongue.&lt;SEP&gt;The oropharynx is the part of the throat that includes the back of the roof of the mouth.&lt;SEP&gt;The oropharynx is the back part of the throat, including the soft palate, tonsils, and base of the tongue.&lt;SEP&gt;The oropharynx is the middle part of the pharynx, including the soft palate, tonsils, and base of the tongue.&lt;SEP&gt;Oropharynx is a part of the throat that is not easily visible when opening the mouth.&lt;SEP&gt;The oropharynx is the part of the throat behind the mouth, which is difficult to visually inspect without special tools.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839641</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dental Exam">
      <data key="d0">Dental Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A Dental Exam is a routine check-up to evaluate oral health, especially important for patients with head and neck cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A dental exam is part of the diagnostic process, often including x-rays or CT scans to evaluate oral health.&lt;SEP&gt;A dental exam involves assessing oral health, including teeth, gums, and jaw structure, often required before cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A dental exam is performed to assess oral health before and during cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Dental exam refers to the process of checking the health of the jaw, teeth, and gums, especially for patients with head and neck cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
