      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nicotine">
      <data key="d0">Nicotine</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nicotine is a chemical found in tobacco that causes addiction and makes people want to continue smoking. It is a substance found in tobacco products and e-cigarettes that can contribute to cancer development and affect treatment efficacy. Nicotine is an addictive chemical found in tobacco products that contributes to smoking and vaping dependence. It is a chemical found in tobacco products that causes addiction and withdrawal symptoms. Nicotine is the chemical in tobacco that causes addiction and makes it difficult to quit smoking or vaping. Nicotine is a chemical found in tobacco that is responsible for the addictive properties of smoking and vaping. Nicotine is a chemical compound found in tobacco that is addictive and contributes to smoking dependence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839642</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Distress Screening">
      <data key="d0">Distress Screening</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Distress Screening is a process used to assess emotional and psychological well-being in cancer patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Distress screening is a process to identify and address emotional and psychological challenges faced by patients with cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Distress screening is a process to assess a patient's emotional and psychological well-being during cancer care.&lt;SEP&gt;Distress screening is a method used to assess emotional and psychological distress in cancer patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Distress screening is a process to identify and address emotional or psychological distress in patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Distress screening is a process to evaluate emotional and psychological distress in individuals diagnosed with cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Distress screening is a process used to assess the emotional and psychological state of a cancer patient.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839642</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Support and Counseling">
      <data key="d0">Support and Counseling</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Support and counseling are resources available to help individuals cope with the emotional challenges of a cancer diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Support and counseling are available services to help patients deal with the emotional impact of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839642</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Biopsy is a medical procedure involving the removal of tissue or fluid samples for examination to diagnose diseases, particularly cancer. It is commonly used to confirm the presence of cancerous cells, determine the nature of tumors, and guide treatment plans. The procedure typically involves taking a small sample of tissue, which is then analyzed under a microscope or in a laboratory to identify abnormalities. Biopsy is a critical diagnostic tool in oncology, used to detect various types of cancer, including lymphoma, Hodgkin Lymphoma, pancreatic cancer, bone cancer, anal cancer, and gliomas. It may also be employed to assess whether cancer has spread to nearby areas, such as lymph nodes. In some cases, biopsies are performed during initial surgery or before chemotherapy. The process can be carried out using different methods, including fine-needle aspiration, core needle biopsy, or surgical excision. Biopsy is also used to diagnose non-cancerous conditions and to confirm or rule out the presence of disease. The procedure is essential in determining the appropriate course of treatment based on the type and stage of the condition. Biopsy is often performed as part of a broader diagnostic evaluation and is considered a standard practice in modern medicine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839642</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Eye Exam">
      <data key="d0">Eye Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An eye exam is a medical evaluation used to assess vision and eye health.&lt;SEP&gt;An eye exam is a procedure used to detect signs of lymphoma in the eyes, particularly vitreoretinal lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;An eye exam might be recommended for patients with nasopharyngeal cancer to check for any effects on the eyes.&lt;SEP&gt;An eye exam checks the health of the nerves in the back of the eyes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839642</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Smoking">
      <data key="d0">Smoking</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Smoking is the act of inhaling and exhaling tobacco smoke, which increases the risk of various cancers and complicates treatment. It is a behavior that increases the risk of developing various cancers, including small cell lung cancer (SCLC), bladder cancer, prostate cancer, cervical cancer, and anal cancer. Smoking is identified as the primary cause of SCLC, with most patients having a history of cigarette use. It is also the greatest risk factor for developing bladder cancer, contributing to about half of all cases. Additionally, smoking is a risk factor for developing and dying from prostate cancer and is associated with increased toxicity and negative impacts on treatment outcomes. Smoking can interfere with the effectiveness of cancer treatments and impact treatment outcomes. It is a harmful habit that increases cancer risk and should be avoided or quit. Smoking is the act of inhaling and exhaling the fumes of burning tobacco, which can lead to various health issues. It is a lifestyle factor that increases the risk of anal cancer by weakening the immune system. Smoking is a risk factor that increases the likelihood of developing cervical cancer. A habit that can be quit with the help of counseling provided by doctors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839642</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Endocrine Tests">
      <data key="d0">Endocrine Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Endocrine Tests are medical examinations to evaluate hormone levels, particularly in the thyroid and pituitary glands.&lt;SEP&gt;Endocrine tests are blood tests used to check hormone levels, particularly after radiation therapy to the head and neck.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839643</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hearing Test">
      <data key="d0">Hearing Test</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A Hearing Test is a diagnostic procedure to assess hearing ability and identify potential hearing loss.&lt;SEP&gt;A hearing test (audiogram) is part of the diagnostic process to assess auditory function.&lt;SEP&gt;A hearing test measures a patient's ability to hear and may be part of the diagnostic process for head and neck cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A hearing test is a procedure to determine if there is any hearing loss and to identify the type and severity of the loss.&lt;SEP&gt;A hearing test (audiogram) is conducted to evaluate potential hearing loss caused by cancer or treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A hearing test is used to determine if there is hearing loss caused by head and neck tumors or their treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839643</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nutrition Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Nutrition Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A Nutrition Assessment is a process to evaluate dietary needs and ensure proper nutrition before treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A nutrition assessment is a process where a nutrition expert evaluates a patient's dietary needs before cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Nutrition assessment involves meeting with a nutrition expert to plan adequate nutrition before cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839643</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Speech and Swallowing Assessment">
      <data key="d0">Speech and Swallowing Assessment</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">A Speech and Swallowing Assessment evaluates a patient's ability to speak and swallow, often conducted before and after treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Speech and swallowing assessment is conducted to evaluate the ability to speak and swallow before and after treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839643</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contrast Agent">
      <data key="d0">Contrast Agent</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Contrast Agent is a substance used in imaging tests to enhance the visibility of internal structures. It is typically injected into the bloodstream to improve the clarity of images and highlight areas of interest, such as cancerous tissues. Contrast agents are commonly used during magnetic resonance imaging (MRI), where substances like gadolinium may be employed to emphasize specific regions. The primary purpose of a contrast agent is to make internal structures more distinct in medical imaging, aiding in diagnosis and treatment planning. These agents are administered through injection, often into a vein, to ensure effective enhancement of the imaging process. The term "contrast agent" refers to various chemicals designed to improve the quality of diagnostic images by increasing the differentiation between tissues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839643</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Health Care Provider">
      <data key="d0">Health Care Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Health Care Provider is a professional or institution that delivers medical care and treatment to patients. This entity encompasses both individual medical professionals and organizations that provide health-related services. A health care provider is a medical professional who offers advice, diagnosis, and treatment for health conditions, including specific diseases such as lung cancer and breast cancer. They are responsible for conducting exams, discussing test results with patients, and providing medical guidance. Health Care Providers are also tasked with diagnosing and treating patients, using special tools when necessary, such as those used to examine areas of the throat. In addition to individual practitioners, this term may refer to teams of professionals working together to deliver comprehensive care. Health Care Providers are defined as medical professionals or institutions that offer medical services and advice, and they play a critical role in the health care system by ensuring that patients receive appropriate care and support. The responsibilities of a health care provider include not only diagnosing and treating medical conditions but also offering ongoing medical guidance and support throughout the course of treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839645</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Head and Neck Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Head and Neck Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Head and Neck Cancer refers to a group of cancers that develop in the head or neck area, including the mouth, throat, voice box, jaw, teeth, gums, lymph nodes, oropharynx, nasopharynx, and larynx. It is a type of cancer that affects the head and neck region, influencing various bodily functions and requiring specialized care. These cancers can be influenced by factors such as smoking and vaping, which may impact treatment outcomes. Head and Neck Cancer is characterized by its ability to affect multiple structures within the head and neck, often necessitating complex surgical procedures. The condition encompasses malignancies that arise in different parts of the head and neck, with variations in affected areas depending on the specific type of cancer. Overall, it is a broad category of cancers that require multidisciplinary approaches for diagnosis, treatment, and management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839645</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Performance Status">
      <data key="d0">Performance Status</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Performance Status is a measure of a patient's overall health and ability to perform daily activities. It is an assessment of a patient's overall physical condition and general fitness, reflecting their capacity to carry out routine tasks. This metric is used in cancer care and treatment planning, as it helps evaluate a patient's general health and influences decisions regarding medical interventions. Performance status evaluates a patient's ability to perform daily activities, which serves as an indicator of their overall well-being. It is also referred to as a measure of a person’s general health and ability to perform daily tasks, with its application extending to clinical settings where treatment strategies are determined based on the patient's functional capacity. The term is consistently used to describe a patient's physical condition and ability to perform daily activities, with variations in phrasing but no significant differences in meaning across descriptions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839645</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fertility">
      <data key="d0">Fertility</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fertility refers to the ability to conceive and have children, which is a fundamental aspect of reproductive health. This definition is consistently mentioned across multiple descriptions, with slight variations in wording such as "conceive and bear children" or "conceive or produce offspring." Fertility can be affected by various factors, particularly cancer treatments. These include chemotherapy, radiation therapy, and specific treatments like those for chronic myeloid leukemia (CML). The impact of these treatments on fertility may vary depending on the type, duration, and intensity of the therapy. Some descriptions highlight that fertility issues can arise as a long-term side effect, especially following radiation therapy for conditions such as anal cancer. Overall, fertility is recognized as a critical element of reproductive capability, with significant implications for individuals undergoing cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
