    <node id="Fertility Preservation">
      <data key="d0">Fertility Preservation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Fertility Preservation is a process that helps maintain the ability to have children after cancer treatment. It refers to various methods and strategies designed to protect or preserve a person's reproductive capabilities, either before or after undergoing cancer treatment. These methods aim to ensure that individuals retain the option of having children despite the potential fertility-threatening effects of cancer therapies. Fertility preservation includes approaches that help maintain the ability to have children both before and after cancer treatment, with some descriptions emphasizing the importance of acting prior to treatment. The primary goal of these methods is to safeguard reproductive health so that individuals can still conceive or have biological children following their cancer care. Different descriptions use slightly varied terminology, such as "protect," "maintain," or "preserve," but all point to the same overarching objective: supporting future parenthood for those affected by cancer. The focus is consistently on the ability to have children, highlighting the importance of reproductive options in the context of cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839647</data>
      <data key="d6" />
