    <node id="Intrauterine Device">
      <data key="d0">Intrauterine Device</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An Intrauterine Device is a form of long-acting birth control inserted into the uterus to prevent pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;An intrauterine device is a form of birth control that is placed in the uterus.&lt;SEP&gt;An intrauterine device is a form of birth control recommended for patients undergoing cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;An intrauterine device (IUD) is a small, T-shaped device placed in the uterus to prevent pregnancy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839648</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Barrier Methods">
      <data key="d0">Barrier Methods</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Barrier Methods include condoms, diaphragms, cervical caps, and the contraceptive sponge used to prevent pregnancy.&lt;SEP&gt;Barrier methods are forms of contraception such as condoms, diaphragms, and cervical caps.&lt;SEP&gt;Barrier methods are forms of contraception such as condoms, diaphragms, cervical caps, and contraceptive sponges.&lt;SEP&gt;Barrier methods are contraceptive techniques that physically prevent sperm from reaching the egg.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839648</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Condoms">
      <data key="d0">Condoms</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Condoms are barrier methods of birth control used to prevent pregnancy and sexually transmitted infections.&lt;SEP&gt;Condoms are a type of barrier method used for contraception.&lt;SEP&gt;Condoms are thin coverings worn on the penis to prevent pregnancy and sexually transmitted infections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839648</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Imaging Tests">
      <data key="d0">Imaging Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Imaging Tests are medical procedures that create visual representations of the inside of the body for diagnostic purposes. These tests use various technologies, such as X-rays, CT scans, MRIs, and PET/CT, to generate images of internal structures. Imaging Tests are used to visualize the adrenal glands, esophagus, and other internal organs, helping to detect abnormalities, tumors, and signs of cancer. They play a critical role in assessing cancer stages, determining whether cancer has spread, and guiding treatment planning. Imaging Tests are also employed to detect leukemia and other conditions outside the bone marrow, as well as to evaluate tumor location and metastasis. In addition to cancer detection, these procedures help diagnose a wide range of medical conditions by providing detailed views of the body's internal structures. Doctors may order Imaging Tests to check if cancer has returned or to identify the presence of cancerous tissues. Overall, Imaging Tests serve as essential tools in modern medicine for visualizing internal body structures and supporting accurate diagnosis and treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
