    <node id="Clinical Stage">
      <data key="d0">Clinical Stage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Clinical Stage is a rating given before any treatment, based on physical exams, biopsies, and imaging tests. It represents an initial assessment of cancer, aimed at determining how far the disease has spread prior to the initiation of therapy. The clinical stage is considered a best guess of the extent of cancer, derived from testing conducted before surgery. This staging process involves evaluating findings from various diagnostic methods, including physical examinations and other tests, to provide a comprehensive understanding of the patient's condition. Clinical stage (c) refers specifically to this pre-treatment evaluation, which plays a critical role in guiding subsequent treatment decisions. The information gathered during this phase helps medical professionals develop an appropriate plan for managing the disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d8e20e6004dd43ae0f68185383b594d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e4e845dfd1390f7f94cfb11bee1526</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839652</data>
