    <node id="Immunophenotyping">
      <data key="d0">Immunophenotyping</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Immunophenotyping is a process that identifies markers on cells, particularly in the immune system.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunophenotyping is a process that uses antibodies to detect the presence or absence of white blood cell antigens called biomarkers.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunophenotyping is a technique used to identify and classify cells based on their surface markers.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunophenotyping is a process that identifies specific markers on white blood cells using antibodies.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunophenotyping is a laboratory test used to identify specific proteins on the surface of cells to help diagnose lymphomas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839652</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin Exam">
      <data key="d0">Skin Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A skin exam is performed to check for suspicious lesions that may indicate skin cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A skin exam is a medical procedure used to monitor for the return of skin cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A skin exam is a physical examination of the skin to detect lesions or abnormalities associated with lymphomas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
