    <node id="Bladder Wall">
      <data key="d0">Bladder Wall</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Bladder wall is the structure of the bladder composed of four main layers.&lt;SEP&gt;The bladder wall is the structure that forms the inner lining of the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839655</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inner Lining">
      <data key="d0">Inner Lining</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Inner lining refers to the urothelial layer of the bladder wall.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839655</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Connective Tissue Layer">
      <data key="d0">Connective Tissue Layer</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Connective tissue layer is the second layer of the bladder wall, located beneath the inner lining.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
