    <node id="Hard Palate">
      <data key="d0">Hard Palate</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The hard palate is the bony part of the roof of the mouth, forming the upper boundary of the oral cavity.&lt;SEP&gt;The hard palate is the bony roof of the mouth, which is a potential site for mouth cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The hard palate is the rigid, anterior portion of the roof of the mouth.&lt;SEP&gt;The hard palate is a bony structure in the mouth that can be invaded by advanced throat cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The hard palate is the bony structure forming the roof of the mouth, located above the nasal cavity and connecting to the pharynx.</data>
