    <node id="Catheter">
      <data key="d0">Catheter</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A catheter is a thin, long tube used to deliver systemic therapy, fluids, and blood products into the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A catheter is a medical device used to administer treatment, tailored to individual patient needs.&lt;SEP&gt;A catheter is a thin tube used to deliver chemotherapy directly into the abdomen.&lt;SEP&gt;A catheter is a thin tube used to deliver systemic therapy, fluids, and blood products into the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Catheter is a thin tube used to drain urine from the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A catheter is inserted into the stoma to drain urine from the Indiana Pouch several times a day.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
