    <node id="White Blood Cell Count">
      <data key="d0">White Blood Cell Count</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">White blood cell count is a factor in determining the dose of cytarabine (Ara-C).&lt;SEP&gt;White Blood Cell Count is a measure of the number of white blood cells in the blood.&lt;SEP&gt;White blood cell count is a medical measurement used to monitor CLL progression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839667</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Oncologist">
      <data key="d0">Medical Oncologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Medical Oncologist is a doctor who specializes in treating cancer using systemic therapies such as chemotherapy, targeted therapy, and immunotherapy. These treatments are typically administered through medications and are designed to attack cancer cells throughout the body. Medical Oncologists often work closely with other specialists to coordinate comprehensive cancer care. They are trained to manage various types of cancer, including thyroid cancer, and play a key role in developing treatment plans tailored to individual patients. The role involves not only administering treatments but also monitoring patient progress and managing side effects. Medical Oncologists are medical doctors who focus on the use of drug-based therapies to treat cancer, distinguishing them from surgical and radiation oncologists. Their expertise includes understanding the complexities of different cancer types and selecting the most effective therapeutic approaches. Overall, Medical Oncologists are central figures in the multidisciplinary team that provides cancer care.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839667</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Spinal Fluid">
      <data key="d0">Spinal Fluid</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Spinal fluid is a clear liquid that surrounds the brain and spinal cord, providing protection and nourishment.&lt;SEP&gt;Spinal fluid is a clear liquid that surrounds the brain and spinal cord, providing protection and nutrients.&lt;SEP&gt;Spinal Fluid is the fluid that surrounds the spine and brain.&lt;SEP&gt;Spinal fluid is a clear liquid that surrounds the brain and spinal cord, used as a route for intrathecal chemotherapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
