    <node id="Methyl Groups">
      <data key="d0">Methyl Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Methyl Groups are molecules found in DNA that can affect gene expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Methyl groups are chemical structures found in DNA that can block gene expression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839667</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genes">
      <data key="d0">Genes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Genes are segments of DNA that contain instructions for the development and function of cells, influencing traits and disease susceptibility.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes are coded instructions for proteins in cells, and mutations can affect their function.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes are segments of DNA that contain instructions for making proteins and are responsible for hereditary traits.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes are segments of DNA that contain instructions for making proteins.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes are segments of DNA that contain instructions for making proteins and are sometimes altered in cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes are the basic units of heredity that control cellular functions and can be altered in cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Genes are segments of DNA that contain instructions for making proteins and determining traits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839667</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Leukemic Blasts">
      <data key="d0">Leukemic Blasts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Leukemic Blasts are abnormal white blood cells that multiply rapidly in AML.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
