    <node id="Indiana Pouch">
      <data key="d0">Indiana Pouch</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Indiana Pouch is a urinary diversion technique developed by surgeons at Indiana University, using a section of the small intestine to connect to a stoma in the abdomen.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839668</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Small Intestine">
      <data key="d0">Small Intestine</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The small intestine is located near the liver and is involved in the digestive process.&lt;SEP&gt;The small intestine is a long, narrow tube where most nutrient absorption occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;The small intestine is a part of the digestive system where most nutrient absorption occurs.&lt;SEP&gt;The small intestine is used to create a connection between the pouch and the stoma in the Indiana Pouch procedure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839668</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stoma">
      <data key="d0">Stoma</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A stoma is an opening created in the abdomen for waste to exit the body, often part of a colostomy.&lt;SEP&gt;A stoma is an opening created on the abdomen to allow stool to exit the body during a colostomy.&lt;SEP&gt;Stoma is an opening created in the abdomen to allow urine to exit the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A stoma is an opening in the abdominal wall that allows urine to exit the body, connected to the Indiana Pouch.&lt;SEP&gt;A stoma is an opening on the abdomen created during a colostomy for stool to exit the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839668</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="One-Way Valve">
      <data key="d0">One-Way Valve</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A one-way valve made from part of the intestine prevents urine from flowing out of the stoma in the Indiana Pouch system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839668</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bandage">
      <data key="d0">Bandage</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A small bandage can be used to cover the stoma in the Indiana Pouch procedure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839668</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urinary Diversion">
      <data key="d0">Urinary Diversion</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Urinary diversion is a surgical procedure that creates an alternative pathway for urine to exit the body after bladder removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Urinary diversion refers to the surgical procedure that reroutes urine flow, such as the Indiana Pouch method.&lt;SEP&gt;Urinary diversion is a surgical procedure that creates a new pathway for urine to leave the body after bladder removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Urinary diversion is a surgical procedure that reroutes urine flow after bladder removal, often causing long-term complications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839668</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Intravesical Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Intravesical Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Intravesical therapy is a treatment administered directly into the bladder, often used in combination with TURBT.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravesical therapy involves filling the bladder with medication to destroy cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravesical therapy involves delivering medicine directly into the bladder to destroy cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravesical therapy involves administering cancer medication directly into the bladder through a catheter.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravesical therapy is a treatment method where medication is placed directly into the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839669</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TURBT">
      <data key="d0">TURBT</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">TURBT stands for Transurethral Resection of Bladder Tumor, a surgical procedure to remove tumors from the bladder lining.&lt;SEP&gt;TURBT is a procedure that examines and removes tumors on the bladder wall.&lt;SEP&gt;Transurethral resection of bladder tumor (TURBT) is a surgical procedure to remove visible bladder cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;TURBT is a surgical procedure to remove visible cancer from the bladder, often used in trimodal therapy for bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839669</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bacillus Calmette-Guérin">
      <data key="d0">Bacillus Calmette-Guérin</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Bacillus Calmette-Guérin (BCG) is a weak bacterium used in intravesical therapy to stimulate the immune system against bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839669</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Intravesical BCG">
      <data key="d0">Intravesical BCG</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Intravesical BCG therapy involves placing a weakened bacterium directly into the bladder to treat bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839669</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Intravesical Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d0">Intravesical Chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Intravesical chemotherapy delivers chemotherapy drugs directly into the bladder to target cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Intravesical chemotherapy is a localized treatment that affects only the inside of the bladder, typically used for early-stage bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839669</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BCG Shortage">
      <data key="d0">BCG Shortage</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">BCG shortage refers to the limited availability of Bacillus Calmette-Guérin for treating bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839669</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="DNA">
      <data key="d0">DNA</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">DNA is a molecule that contains genetic information and is found in the cells of all living organisms. It serves as the genetic material responsible for directing the development, functioning, growth, and reproduction of all known living organisms. DNA contains instructions for biological development and function, including the production of proteins, which are essential for cellular activities. The genetic information stored in DNA is packaged into chromosomes within cells, particularly in the nucleus. This genetic material is found in every cell of the body and carries the instructions necessary for building and maintaining an organism. DNA is analyzed using methods such as next-generation sequencing (NGS) and polymerase chain reaction (PCR), which allow scientists to study its structure and function in detail. As the fundamental carrier of hereditary traits, DNA plays a central role in genetics and molecular biology, providing the blueprint for life.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839669</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Side Effects">
      <data key="d0">Side Effects</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Side Effects are unintended reactions or effects of medical treatments, often occurring alongside the desired therapeutic effect. These effects can vary depending on the type of treatment, such as medications, chemotherapy, surgery, radiation therapy, or other medical procedures. Side effects may be physical or psychological and can include a wide range of symptoms, such as fatigue, nausea, infections, hair loss, mouth sores, and emotional discomfort. They are commonly associated with cancer treatments but can also occur with other forms of medical care. In some cases, side effects may be temporary, while in others they may persist and require management by the care team. These unintended consequences can impact a patient's quality of life, health, and daily activities. Some descriptions specifically mention that side effects may occur during chemotherapy or other targeted therapies, such as intravesical treatments. Overall, side effects are an important consideration in medical treatment planning and patient care.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839669</data>
      <data key="d6" />
