    <node id="Lymph">
      <data key="d0">Lymph</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymph is a clear fluid that circulates through the lymphatic system, helping to fight infections and transport waste products. It carries infection-fighting white blood cells throughout the body, playing a key role in the immune response. Lymph is also responsible for carrying other substances, including cells that help fight infections, and it drains through lymphatic vessels into lymph nodes. Additionally, lymph can carry cancer cells, making it an important factor in the spread of certain diseases. The fluid is essential for maintaining the body's defense mechanisms and removing waste materials from tissues. Overall, lymph serves as a vital medium within the lymphatic system, supporting both immune function and cellular health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839676</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Colon Cancers">
      <data key="d0">Colon Cancers</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Colon cancers are malignant tumors that originate in the colon and often start from polyps.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839676</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Testing">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Genetic Testing is a medical procedure used to analyze a person's DNA for genetic mutations, variations, or abnormalities. It involves examining inherited DNA changes that may increase the risk of developing certain diseases, including cancer. Genetic testing can detect gene mutations, chromosomal abnormalities, or other genetic alterations that are linked to specific conditions or disorders. The process typically uses blood or saliva samples and is used to assess an individual's predisposition to inherited genetic conditions.  

Genetic Testing is also used in the context of cancer care, where it identifies genetic changes in leukemia cells or other cancer-related mutations to guide treatment planning and prognosis. For example, it can detect BRCA mutations or other inherited genetic markers that contribute to cancer risk. While similar to tumor mutation testing, genetic testing specifically focuses on inherited DNA mutations rather than those acquired in cancer cells.  

The term "Genetic Testing" encompasses a broad category of tests that analyze DNA to identify mutations associated with various diseases. These tests are used both for diagnostic purposes and for assessing the likelihood of developing hereditary conditions. Genetic Testing is a key tool in personalized medicine, helping to inform medical decisions based on an individual's genetic profile.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839676</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Questions to Ask">
      <data key="d0">Questions to Ask</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Questions to Ask is a section in a book or publication that helps patients prepare for discussions with their care team. It is typically found at the end of each chapter and provides suggested questions for patients to ask their care team about their diagnosis, treatment, and overall care. The purpose of this section is to assist patients in gathering information, engaging with their healthcare team, and making informed decisions about their health. Some descriptions specify that it is designed to help patients discuss their care with their team, while others mention that it focuses on topics such as CLL or cancer care. Overall, the section serves as a resource for patients to better understand their medical situation and communicate effectively with their healthcare providers. The content may vary slightly depending on the chapter or context, but the core goal remains consistent: to support patients in asking the right questions during their care journey.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c5bc83f5f4f3e29b7f0a6f4787c3ad83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839676</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Polypectomy">
      <data key="d0">Polypectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Polypectomy is a minor surgical procedure used to remove polyps during a colonoscopy.&lt;SEP&gt;Polypectomy is a minor surgical procedure performed during a colonoscopy to remove polyps.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
