    <node id="Mismatch Repair Deficiency">
      <data key="d0">Mismatch Repair Deficiency</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mismatch repair deficiency is a genetic condition that increases the risk of certain cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;Mismatch repair deficiency (dMMR) is a biomarker found in some colon cancers that influences treatment planning.&lt;SEP&gt;Mismatch repair deficiency is a genetic condition that can lead to certain types of cancer, including colon cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Mismatch repair deficiency (dMMR) is a condition associated with certain cancers and may indicate response to immunotherapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839677</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Colon Cancer Screening">
      <data key="d0">Colon Cancer Screening</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Colon cancer screening involves tests to detect early signs of cancer or precancerous conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
