    <node id="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Cervical Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cervical Cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the cells of the cervix, which is part of the female reproductive system. It is primarily caused by human papillomavirus (HPV) infections, with certain high-risk HPV strains being strongly associated with the development of this cancer. Cervical Cancer can spread to nearby lymph nodes and is typically staged using the FIGO system, which helps guide treatment decisions. Diagnosis of Cervical Cancer involves various medical procedures, including cervical biopsy and other tests. The cancer has multiple stages and is treated using combined therapies, such as surgery, radiation, and chemotherapy, depending on the stage and patient condition. Cervical Cancer is also discussed in the context of surveillance and treatment, with early detection through screening playing a critical role in improving outcomes. While most descriptions focus on its origin in the cervix and association with HPV, one description mentions that it may be screened for after an anal cancer diagnosis, though this connection is less commonly emphasized in standard literature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839683</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Distress">
      <data key="d0">Distress</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Distress is an unpleasant experience that can have mental, physical, social, or spiritual effects, and may include feelings of sadness, fear, helplessness, worry, anger, and guilt.&lt;SEP&gt;Distress is an unpleasant experience that can have mental, physical, social, or spiritual effects, often associated with a cancer diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Distress refers to emotional or psychological stress experienced by cancer patients and their caregivers.&lt;SEP&gt;Distress is a state of emotional suffering, commonly experienced by cancer survivors and addressed through mental health resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Emotional or psychological stress experienced by cancer survivors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
