    <node id="Imaging">
      <data key="d0">Imaging</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Imaging is a diagnostic technique used to visualize internal structures of the body. It encompasses various medical methods, including X-rays, MRIs, CT scans, and PET scans, which are employed to detect abnormalities, such as tumors and cancer. Imaging plays a critical role in cancer detection, staging, and treatment planning. For instance, it is used to stage pancreatic cancer and determine appropriate treatment options. Additionally, imaging helps in detecting cancer spread, assessing the extent of the disease, and monitoring for recurrence after treatment. Specific applications include visualizing the brain to detect gliomas, the bladder to evaluate cancer involvement, and internal structures to analyze cancer progression. Imaging is also utilized to guide treatment decisions by providing detailed insights into the body's internal conditions. Overall, imaging serves as an essential tool in both diagnosis and management of various medical conditions, particularly in oncology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e9a7fe3b15f3289198c7114b44890dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
