    <node id="Karyotype">
      <data key="d0">Karyotype</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A karyotype is a picture of chromosomes that shows abnormalities such as missing, extra, or rearranged pieces.&lt;SEP&gt;A karyotype is a visual representation of an individual's chromosomes, used to detect abnormalities such as extra, missing, or rearranged chromosomes.&lt;SEP&gt;A karyotype is a visual representation of chromosomes used to identify abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Karyotype is a test that shows defects in chromosomes and may reveal complex changes in CLL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
