    <node id="Next-Generation Sequencing">
      <data key="d0">Next-Generation Sequencing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Next-generation sequencing (NGS) is a method used to determine parts of a person’s DNA sequence and detect mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;Next-generation sequencing (NGS) is a DNA analysis method that provides detailed genetic information and can identify mutations that other methods might miss.&lt;SEP&gt;Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS) is a detailed method for analyzing DNA sequences to detect mutations.&lt;SEP&gt;Next-generation sequencing (NGS) is a high-throughput method used to analyze the DNA sequence of cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Next-generation sequencing (NGS) is a comprehensive method for analyzing multiple genetic markers simultaneously.&lt;SEP&gt;Next-generation sequencing is a technique used to analyze DNA sequences in detail.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839687</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Polymerase Chain Reaction">
      <data key="d0">Polymerase Chain Reaction</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is a method used to amplify DNA for mutation detection.&lt;SEP&gt;Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is a technique used to amplify DNA or RNA, allowing for the detection of rare abnormal cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is a technique used to amplify DNA for analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Polymerase chain reaction is a technique used to amplify DNA or RNA samples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839687</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anesthesia">
      <data key="d0">Anesthesia</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Anesthesia is a medical treatment that induces a temporary loss of sensation or awareness to prevent pain during surgical procedures. It is commonly used to ensure patients do not feel pain or are unaware during medical interventions. Anesthesia can be administered as a medication to numb specific areas of the body or to induce sleep, depending on the type and purpose of the procedure. The primary goal of anesthesia is to eliminate pain and discomfort, allowing for safe and effective medical treatments. It is a medical technique that can cause a loss of sensation or unconsciousness, often required for procedures such as direct laryngoscopy or other invasive surgeries. Anesthesia involves the use of drugs to achieve these effects, and it plays a critical role in modern surgical practice. Different types of anesthesia may be employed, including local, regional, and general, each tailored to the specific needs of the patient and the nature of the procedure. Overall, anesthesia is essential for ensuring patient comfort and safety during medical procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839687</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Real-Time PCR">
      <data key="d0">Real-Time PCR</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Real-time PCR is a type of PCR used to detect gene rearrangements, such as PML::RARA, aiding in diagnosis and treatment monitoring.&lt;SEP&gt;Real-Time PCR is a technique used to detect gene rearrangements such as PML::RARA.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
