    <node id="Leukemia">
      <data key="d0">Leukemia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Leukemia is a type of cancer affecting blood and bone marrow, capable of spreading to other organs like the liver, spleen, and skin.&lt;SEP&gt;Leukemia is a type of cancer that affects the blood and bone marrow.&lt;SEP&gt;Leukemia is a type of blood cancer characterized by the overproduction of immature lymphocytes called lymphoblasts.&lt;SEP&gt;Leukemia is a type of cancer that affects the blood and bone marrow, leading to the overproduction of abnormal white blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Leukemia is a type of cancer that starts in the bone marrow and affects blood cell production.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839688</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PML::RARA">
      <data key="d0">PML::RARA</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">PML::RARA is an abnormal fusion gene found in a rare subtype of AML called APL.&lt;SEP&gt;PML::RARA is a specific gene rearrangement detected by real-time PCR, associated with certain types of leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;PML::RARA is an abnormal fusion gene found in Acute Promyelocytic Leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;PML::RARA is a gene rearrangement commonly found in certain types of leukemia.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc31077c053f79ff82959575d335956&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839688</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="QTc">
      <data key="d0">QTc</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">QTc is a measure of the time it takes for the heart muscle to recharge between beats, with prolonged intervals indicating potential cardiac risks.&lt;SEP&gt;QTc is a measurement of the time between the start of the Q wave and the end of the T wave in the heart's electrical cycle, indicating potential heart rhythm issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839688</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contrast">
      <data key="d0">Contrast</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Contrast is a substance used in medical imaging to enhance the visibility of internal structures. It is commonly employed in various imaging tests, including CT scans, to improve image clarity and help doctors better visualize organs, blood vessels, and other internal features. Contrast can be administered in different ways, such as injection into a vein or consumption orally, depending on the type of imaging procedure and the area being examined. The primary purpose of contrast is to make the images clearer, allowing for more accurate diagnosis and assessment. It is an essential tool in many diagnostic imaging procedures, particularly those involving computed tomography (CT) scans. The method of administration varies based on the specific test and the part of the body being imaged. Despite slight variations in phrasing across descriptions, all emphasize the role of contrast as a critical component in enhancing the quality and interpretability of medical images.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-925a474b4538dda470bfd817f9d9a17d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839688</data>
