    <node id="MRI">
      <data key="d0">MRI</data>
      <data key="d1">equipment</data>
      <data key="d2">Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI) is a medical imaging technique that uses magnetic fields and radio waves to create detailed images of the body's internal structures. It is widely used in diagnostic medicine for visualizing soft tissues, organs, and other internal body parts without the use of ionizing radiation. MRI works by aligning the hydrogen atoms in the body with a strong magnetic field and then using radio waves to excite these atoms, which then emit signals that are processed by a computer to generate images. The process is non-invasive and can provide high-resolution images that are particularly useful for detecting abnormalities such as brain swelling from leukemia or primary central nervous system lymphoma. MRI is also employed in cancer assessment, including evaluating cancer recurrence and guiding treatment decisions. Additionally, it is used to guide the placement of brachytherapy applicators and to monitor conditions like anal cancer recurrence when combined with other imaging techniques such as CT scans. MRI is sometimes referred to as Magnetic Resonance Imaging, with both terms being used interchangeably in medical contexts. The technique is especially effective for visualizing the brain and spinal cord, making it an essential tool in neurological diagnostics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839690</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pap Test">
      <data key="d0">Pap Test</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Pap test is a procedure used to detect cervical cancer or pre-cancerous changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Pap test is a screening procedure used to detect abnormal cells in the cervix.&lt;SEP&gt;A Pap test is a procedure where cells are scraped from the cervix and tested for HPV, cancer, and cell changes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839690</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="FDG-PET/CT">
      <data key="d0">FDG-PET/CT</data>
      <data key="d1">equipment</data>
      <data key="d2">FDG-PET/CT is a combined imaging technique that uses a radiotracer called fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG) to detect cancerous cells in the body. It integrates positron emission tomography (PET) with computed tomography (CT), providing both functional and anatomical information. This imaging method is widely used to detect and stage various types of cancer, including leukemia outside the blood and bone marrow. FDG-PET/CT is also employed to identify distant metastases in cancer patients, offering detailed diagnostic insights. The technique relies on a radioactive tracer, specifically F-18 fluorodeoxyglucose, which accumulates in areas of high metabolic activity, such as cancer cells. As a specific type of PET/CT scan, FDG-PET/CT combines the strengths of both modalities to enhance diagnostic accuracy and guide treatment planning. It is an essential tool in oncology for evaluating tumor metabolism and localization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839690</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
