    <node id="Fallopian Tubes">
      <data key="d0">Fallopian Tubes</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Fallopian tubes are part of the female reproductive system and can be examined during imaging tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Fallopian tubes are long, thin tubes that connect the ovaries to the uterus, facilitating the movement of eggs.&lt;SEP&gt;The fallopian tubes are structures that may be affected by ovarian cancer, as seen in stages 2A and 2B.&lt;SEP&gt;Fallopian tubes are ducts that carry eggs from the ovaries to the uterus.&lt;SEP&gt;The fallopian tubes are part of the female reproductive system and can be involved in fertility preservation procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
