      <data key="d5">1772839693</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ovaries">
      <data key="d0">Ovaries</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The ovaries are female reproductive organs that produce eggs and hormones. They are part of the female reproductive system and play a critical role in fertility and hormonal regulation. The ovaries are a pair of organs located within the pelvic cavity, responsible for the development and release of eggs during the menstrual cycle. In addition to their role in reproduction, they also produce essential hormones such as estrogen and progesterone, which regulate various physiological functions. The ovaries can be affected by cancer treatments, including chemotherapy and radiation therapy, which may lead to infertility or other long-term health impacts. While the ovaries are generally associated with reproductive functions, they can also develop tumors or other abnormalities, making them a focus of medical attention in gynecological health. Overall, the ovaries are vital components of the female body, influencing both reproductive and endocrine systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5406c28b41e499fad4ae44f2c44fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839693</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Terminal Duct Lobular Units">
      <data key="d0">Terminal Duct Lobular Units</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Terminal duct lobular units are the small structures in the breast where most breast cancers originate.&lt;SEP&gt;Terminal duct lobular units are the structures in the breast where most breast cancers originate.&lt;SEP&gt;Terminal duct lobular units are the structures in the breast where breast cancer originates, consisting of ducts and lobules.</data>
