    <node id="Breast Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Breast Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Breast Cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the breast tissue and can spread to other parts of the body. It is characterized by the uncontrolled growth of abnormal cells in the breast, which may lead to the formation of tumors. The disease can develop in various parts of the breast, including the ducts and lobules, and may involve the surrounding tissues. Breast Cancer can be staged based on factors such as tumor size, lymph node involvement, and whether the cancer has spread beyond the breast. It is a significant health concern, affecting millions of people worldwide, and often requires specific treatment considerations, such as surgery, chemotherapy, radiation therapy, or hormone therapy. Early detection and diagnosis play a critical role in improving outcomes for patients. While the descriptions vary slightly in wording, they all consistently describe Breast Cancer as a malignant condition arising from abnormal cell growth in the breast tissue.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839693</data>
