    </node>
    <node id="Gynecologic Oncologist">
      <data key="d0">Gynecologic Oncologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A gynecologic oncologist is a specialist in treating cancers of the female reproductive system, including ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A gynecologic oncologist is a medical specialist who treats female reproductive cancers through surgery and chemotherapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839693</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gynecologist">
      <data key="d0">Gynecologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A gynecologist is a medical doctor who specializes in the health of the female reproductive system.&lt;SEP&gt;A gynecologist diagnoses and treats diseases of the female reproductive system.&lt;SEP&gt;A gynecologist is a doctor specializing in women's reproductive health and may be part of the cancer care team.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839694</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nurses">
      <data key="d0">Nurses</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Nurses are healthcare professionals who provide direct patient care and support.&lt;SEP&gt;Nurses are healthcare professionals who provide direct patient care and support during cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839694</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Social Workers">
      <data key="d0">Social Workers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Social workers are professionals who offer emotional and practical support to cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839694</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anxiety">
      <data key="d0">Anxiety</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Anxiety is a psychological condition that frequently occurs in individuals diagnosed with cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Anxiety is a common emotional response among cancer patients, often addressed through supportive care.&lt;SEP&gt;A psychological condition that may affect cancer survivors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839694</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Depression">
      <data key="d0">Depression</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Depression is a mental health condition commonly experienced by cancer patients and their caregivers.&lt;SEP&gt;Depression is a mental health condition frequently experienced by cancer patients, requiring support and intervention.&lt;SEP&gt;A mental health condition that may affect cancer survivors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839694</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Navigators">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Navigators</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer navigators are professionals who guide patients through the complexities of cancer care and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839694</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Support Groups">
      <data key="d0">Support Groups</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Support groups provide emotional and social support to patients undergoing cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Support groups are organized gatherings where cancer patients can share experiences and receive emotional support.&lt;SEP&gt;Support groups are organizations providing emotional and practical support to cancer survivors and their families.&lt;SEP&gt;Groups where people with cancer can share experiences and receive emotional support.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Talk Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Talk Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Talk therapy is a form of psychological treatment that helps cancer patients manage emotional distress.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Exercise">
      <data key="d0">Exercise</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Exercise is a factor that can temporarily increase PSA levels, prompting recommendations to avoid it before a PSA test.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise and maintaining a healthy weight may decrease the aggressiveness of prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise is a recommended activity for cancer patients to improve well-being and manage symptoms.&lt;SEP&gt;Exercise is physical activity intended to improve health and fitness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medication">
      <data key="d0">Medication</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Medication is a treatment option used to manage symptoms and conditions related to cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Medication is a substance used to treat or prevent disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Distress During Cancer Care">
      <data key="d0">Distress During Cancer Care</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Distress during cancer care refers to the emotional and psychological stress experienced by patients, requiring supportive interventions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical History">
      <data key="d0">Medical History</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Medical History is a record of a patient's past and current health issues, treatments, medications, and family health background. It is used by care teams to determine appropriate treatments for patients and plays a critical role in the diagnostic process, particularly for conditions such as cancer. This record includes all previous health issues and treatments a patient has experienced, as well as illnesses, treatments, and family health patterns. Medical History serves as a comprehensive overview of an individual's health journey, encompassing both past and current health conditions. It is essential for guiding medical decisions and developing treatment plans tailored to the patient's specific needs. The information contained in a Medical History helps healthcare providers understand the context of a patient’s health, enabling more accurate diagnoses and effective care. This record may also include details about medications and other interventions the patient has received over time. Overall, Medical History is a vital component of patient care, providing a detailed account of health experiences that informs clinical decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Primary Care Physician">
      <data key="d0">Primary Care Physician</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Primary Care Physician is a healthcare provider who manages a patient's overall health and coordinates care. This role involves overseeing patient care, providing general healthcare services, and ensuring that patients receive appropriate medical attention. A Primary Care Physician (PCP) serves as the first point of contact for patients and provides initial care for health issues. They are responsible for maintaining overall health oversight and updating patients on changes in their condition. The primary care physician also coordinates treatment with specialists when necessary, ensuring that patients receive comprehensive healthcare. This healthcare provider manages a patient's overall care and works to integrate various aspects of medical treatment. They play a key role in the care team by managing general health and facilitating communication between different healthcare professionals. The primary care physician is a medical doctor who provides general healthcare and acts as a central figure in the coordination of patient care. Their responsibilities include managing a patient's overall health, coordinating treatment, and working closely with specialists to ensure effective and continuous care.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Care Team">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Care Team</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A cancer care team consists of multiple specialists working together to provide comprehensive treatment for ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The cancer care team is a multidisciplinary group of healthcare professionals responsible for treating and supporting cancer patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer Care Team is a group of healthcare professionals who provide treatment and support for cancer patients.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Family History">
      <data key="d0">Family History</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Family History refers to the health information of blood relatives, which can indicate hereditary risks for diseases such as cancer. It encompasses the medical conditions and diseases present in a person's family members, particularly close and biological relatives. This information is used to assess potential genetic predispositions and can influence disease risk, testing recommendations, and medical evaluations. Family history may include specific conditions such as prostate cancer, bladder cancer, or thyroid cancer, and the presence of these diseases in close relatives can increase an individual's risk of developing similar conditions. It is also described as a record of health issues among a person's blood relatives, which helps identify genetic risks for various diseases. Additionally, family history includes information about health conditions and ancestry within a person's family, providing insights into potential genetic factors. The term is often used in the context of understanding inherited disorders and guiding preventive healthcare measures. Overall, Family History serves as an important tool in evaluating an individual's susceptibility to hereditary diseases and informing medical decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a06038ec84f20e873b9e275a23aea8d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 1A">
      <data key="d0">Stage 1A</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 1A is an early stage of ovarian cancer where cancer is present in one ovary with an intact capsule and no cancer on the outer surface or in ascites.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1A is an early stage of cervical cancer where the tumor is 5 millimeters or smaller.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1A is an early stage of cervical cancer, characterized by cancer confined to the cervix.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 1B1">
      <data key="d0">Stage 1B1</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 1B1 refers to cervical cancer that is larger than 5 mm but smaller than 2 cm.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1B1 is a classification of cervical cancer that indicates cancer has grown into the upper part of the vagina.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1B1 is a sub-stage of Stage 1B cervical cancer, indicating cancer that has grown into the upper part of the vagina.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839695</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 1B2">
      <data key="d0">Stage 1B2</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 1B2 is a stage of cervical cancer where the tumor is between 2 and 4 cm in size.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1B2 is a classification of cervical cancer that indicates cancer has grown more extensively into the upper part of the vagina.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1B2 is a sub-stage of Stage 1B cervical cancer, indicating cancer that has grown further into the vagina.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839696</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 1B3">
      <data key="d0">Stage 1B3</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 1B3 refers to cervical cancer that is larger than 4 cm and confined to the cervix.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1B3 is a sub-stage of Stage 1B cervical cancer, indicating cancer that is larger than 4 cm and may extend beyond the cervix.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839696</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 2A1">
      <data key="d0">Stage 2A1</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 2A1 is a stage of cervical cancer where the tumor is 4 cm or smaller and has grown into the upper vagina.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 2A1 is a sub-stage of Stage 2A cervical cancer, indicating cancer that has grown into the upper part of the vagina.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839696</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bone">
      <data key="d0">Bone</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Bone is a hard, dense tissue that provides structure and protection to the body. It is a living tissue composed of specialized cells, collagen, blood vessels, minerals, and proteins, and it is capable of regrowing. As part of the skeletal system, bone serves as a critical site for various physiological functions. Bone can be affected by cancer metastasis, meaning that cancer from other parts of the body may spread to the bone. Prostate cancer, breast cancer, cervical cancer, liver cancer, and stomach cancer are all known to metastasize to the bone. This makes bone a common site for distant metastasis, as indicated by medical classifications such as "M1b – Metastasis is in the bone or other distant sites." Bone scans are often used to detect such metastatic activity, and imaging procedures are employed to examine bone for signs of cancer. The ability of bone to both support and be affected by cancer highlights its importance in oncology and diagnostic medicine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839696</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 2A2">
      <data key="d0">Stage 2A2</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 2A2 refers to cervical cancer that is larger than 4 cm and has grown into the upper vagina.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 2A2 is a sub-stage of Stage 2A cervical cancer, indicating cancer that is larger than 4 cm and extends into the upper vagina.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839696</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 2B">
      <data key="d0">Stage 2B</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 2B is a stage of ovarian cancer where cancer has spread to other pelvic organs or tissues such as the bladder, colon, or rectum.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 2B is a stage of cervical cancer where the tumor has grown into the parametrium.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 2B is a stage of cervical cancer where cancer has spread to the pelvic wall or lower part of the vagina.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839696</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 3C">
      <data key="d0">Stage 3C</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 3C is a stage of ovarian cancer where cancer is visible on the abdominal lining, with a larger area of cancer and possible involvement of the liver or spleen.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 3C refers to cervical cancer with involvement of pelvic or para-aortic lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-db3a86fc5d439d9bfb3845e468a2a551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b</data>
