    </node>
    <node id="Placebo">
      <data key="d0">Placebo</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A placebo is an inactive substance used in clinical trials to compare the effects of real treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;A placebo is an inactive version of a real medicine used in some clinical trials to compare treatment effects.&lt;SEP&gt;A placebo is an inactive substance or treatment used in clinical trials to compare the effects of real treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;A placebo is a substance or treatment with no therapeutic effect, used as a control in clinical trials.&lt;SEP&gt;A placebo is an inactive substance used in clinical trials to compare the effects of a real treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A placebo is an inactive substance or treatment used in clinical trials to compare the effects of an actual treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-60426652ddf8265bf75caba550026d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
