    <node id="Flow Cytometry">
      <data key="d0">Flow Cytometry</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Flow cytometry is a laboratory technique used to analyze and count specific types of cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Flow cytometry is a technique used to detect subtle differences between types of blood cancers by identifying markers on cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Flow cytometry is a laboratory technique used to analyze and count cells based on their physical and chemical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Flow cytometry is a technique used to analyze the characteristics of cells in a blood sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Flow cytometry is a laboratory technique used to detect and analyze the characteristics of cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839698</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Biomarkers">
      <data key="d0">Biomarkers</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Biomarkers are proteins found on or inside white blood cells that can be targeted in AML treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomarkers are measurable indicators of biological states or conditions, often used in AML diagnosis and treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomarkers are biological indicators that can be used to detect or monitor diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomarkers are molecular characteristics, such as genetic mutations, used to identify and classify diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomarkers are unique features of CLL cells used to guide treatment decisions and are identified through lab tests.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839698</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Immunohistochemistry">
      <data key="d0">Immunohistochemistry</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Immunohistochemistry (IHC) is a staining process used to study the immunophenotype of cells from a biopsy or tissue sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunohistochemistry is a staining technique used to detect specific proteins in tissue samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunohistochemistry is a staining process used to detect receptors in breast cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunohistochemistry (IHC) is a method used to detect specific proteins in tissue samples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839698</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="FLT">
      <data key="d0">FLT</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">FLT is a gene identified in italics, associated with AML and other leukemias.&lt;SEP&gt;FLT refers to a gene associated with certain types of leukemia and is often identified in genetic testing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
