    </node>
    <node id="Skin Punch Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Skin Punch Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">A skin punch biopsy removes a small piece of skin and connective tissue using a hand-held tool, often requiring stitches.&lt;SEP&gt;A skin punch biopsy is a medical procedure where a small piece of skin and connective tissue is removed using a hand-held tool.&lt;SEP&gt;A skin punch biopsy is a procedure to remove a small piece of skin and connective tissue for DNA testing.&lt;SEP&gt;A skin punch biopsy is a procedure that removes a small piece of skin and connective tissue to obtain DNA for genetic testing.&lt;SEP&gt;A skin punch biopsy is a procedure where a small sample of skin is taken for analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
