    </node>
    <node id="Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization">
      <data key="d0">Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization (FISH) uses special dyes to detect small genetic changes in DNA.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization (FISH) is a technique that uses probes to detect specific DNA changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization (FISH) is a lab test used to detect genetic abnormalities such as 17p deletion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
