    <node id="Digestive System">
      <data key="d0">Digestive System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The digestive system is a group of organs that work together to break down food and absorb nutrients.&lt;SEP&gt;The digestive system takes in food, breaks it down, absorbs nutrients, and removes waste from the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The digestive system is a group of organs that work together to break down food, absorb nutrients, and eliminate waste, as described in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;The digestive system is the body's system responsible for breaking down food, absorbing nutrients, and removing waste.&lt;SEP&gt;The digestive system is a collection of organs responsible for breaking down food, absorbing nutrients, and removing waste from the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839703</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Esophagus">
      <data key="d0">Esophagus</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The esophagus is a muscular tube that transports food from the throat to the stomach.&lt;SEP&gt;The esophagus is a muscular tube that carries food and liquid from the throat to the stomach.&lt;SEP&gt;The esophagus is a muscular tube that connects the pharynx to the stomach and is part of the digestive system.&lt;SEP&gt;The esophagus is a muscular tube that connects the mouth to the stomach.&lt;SEP&gt;The esophagus is a muscular tube that transports food and drink from the mouth to the stomach.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839703</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gallbladder">
      <data key="d0">Gallbladder</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The gallbladder is a small, pear-shaped organ found under the liver that stores bile.&lt;SEP&gt;The gallbladder stores bile produced by the liver and releases it into the small intestine during digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;The gallbladder stores and releases bile, which aids in fat digestion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839703</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pancreas">
      <data key="d0">Pancreas</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The pancreas is an organ that produces enzymes for digestion and hormones for regulating blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas is one of the organs that may be affected by metastatic esophageal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas is a gland that plays a role in digestion and blood sugar regulation.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas is a large gland located deep in the abdomen, responsible for producing digestive enzymes and hormones that regulate blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas is an organ located near the liver and is sometimes considered part of the hepatobiliary system.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas produces enzymes for digestion and hormones that regulate blood sugar.&lt;SEP&gt;The pancreas produces digestive enzymes and hormones like insulin.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839703</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chyme">
      <data key="d0">Chyme</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chyme is a semi-fluid mass of partly digested food that passes from the stomach to the small intestine, as explained in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Chyme is a semi-fluid mass of partly digested food that passes from the stomach to the small intestine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5fdcf47f3da06d3e0213112c96eb93d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a</data>
