    <node id="Papillary Thyroid Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Papillary Thyroid Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Papillary thyroid cancer is a common type of thyroid cancer that is usually treated with surgery and radioactive iodine therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Papillary thyroid cancer is the most common type of thyroid cancer, characterized by its papillary structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839705</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Follicular Thyroid Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Follicular Thyroid Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Follicular thyroid cancer is a less common type of thyroid cancer that may require radioactive iodine therapy or surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;Follicular thyroid cancer is a type of thyroid cancer that arises from the follicular cells of the thyroid gland.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839705</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Oncocytic Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Oncocytic Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Oncocytic carcinoma is a rare type of thyroid cancer that involves cells with abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm.&lt;SEP&gt;Oncocytic carcinoma is a rare type of thyroid cancer characterized by cells with abundant mitochondria.&lt;SEP&gt;Oncocytic carcinoma is a rare type of thyroid cancer that contains oncocytic cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839705</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Differentiated Thyroid Cancers">
      <data key="d0">Differentiated Thyroid Cancers</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Differentiated thyroid cancers are a group of thyroid cancers that include papillary, follicular, and oncocytic carcinomas, which tend to grow slowly and have a better prognosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Differentiated thyroid cancers are a group of thyroid cancers that include papillary, follicular, and oncocytic carcinomas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839705</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Active Surveillance">
      <data key="d0">Active Surveillance</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Active surveillance is a management approach for early-stage prostate cancer where regular tests monitor the cancer without immediate treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Active surveillance is a strategy where patients with low-risk cancer are closely monitored without immediate treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Active surveillance is a strategy where patients with low-risk cancer are monitored over time rather than treated immediately.&lt;SEP&gt;Active surveillance is an approach where small, low-risk thyroid cancers are closely monitored instead of being treated immediately.&lt;SEP&gt;Active surveillance is a strategy where small, low-risk thyroid cancers are monitored without immediate treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839706</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thyroid Hormone Replacement Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Thyroid Hormone Replacement Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Thyroid hormone replacement therapy involves administering synthetic thyroid hormones to patients who have had their thyroid gland removed.&lt;SEP&gt;Thyroid hormone replacement therapy involves administering synthetic thyroid hormones to patients with thyroid dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;Thyroid hormone replacement therapy involves administering synthetic thyroid hormones to patients after thyroid surgery to maintain normal hormone levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Thyroid hormone replacement therapy involves administering synthetic thyroid hormones to patients who have had their thyroid removed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
