    <node id="Support System">
      <data key="d0">Support System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A support system is important during diagnosis and treatment, providing assistance with transportation, meals, and emotional support.&lt;SEP&gt;A support system refers to individuals who provide assistance and emotional support during diagnosis and treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A support system is a network of individuals who provide assistance during medical treatment and diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;A support system refers to a network of friends, family members, or peers who provide assistance during diagnosis and treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A support system consists of individuals who provide emotional, physical, and logistical assistance during medical treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;A support system refers to individuals who provide emotional, physical, and logistical assistance during the diagnosis and treatment of a medical condition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64f36a4a5be80c8fa51631db16e52b85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
