      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Friends">
      <data key="d0">Friends</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Friends can offer support by providing transportation, meals, and emotional assistance during the diagnosis and treatment of a medical condition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Family Members">
      <data key="d0">Family Members</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Family members are individuals related by blood or marriage.&lt;SEP&gt;Family members can assist with various tasks such as transportation, meals, and emotional support during the diagnosis and treatment of a medical condition.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Peers">
      <data key="d0">Peers</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Peers can provide support during the diagnosis and treatment of a medical condition, often offering shared experiences and encouragement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Doctor">
      <data key="d0">Doctor</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A doctor is a medical professional who diagnoses and treats illnesses and injuries.&lt;SEP&gt;A doctor is a medical professional who can recommend genetic testing and refer patients to a genetic counselor.&lt;SEP&gt;A doctor is a medical professional who provides healthcare and orders diagnostic tests.&lt;SEP&gt;A doctor is a medical professional who diagnoses and treats patients, playing a key role in interpreting test results and determining treatment plans.&lt;SEP&gt;A medical professional who provides guidance and treatment plans to patients.&lt;SEP&gt;A doctor is a medical professional who diagnoses and treats patients, often providing guidance on treatment options.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Health Care Team">
      <data key="d0">Health Care Team</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The health care team includes doctors, nurses, and other professionals who assist patients in understanding and managing their medical conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The health care team consists of medical professionals who work together to provide comprehensive care and support to patients.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urothelium">
      <data key="d0">Urothelium</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The urothelium is the inner lining of the bladder that prevents urine from leaking back into the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The urothelium is the inner lining of the urinary tract, including the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ureters">
      <data key="d0">Ureters</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The ureters are tubes that carry urine from the kidneys to the bladder.&lt;SEP&gt;Ureters are tubes that carry urine from the kidneys to the bladder.&lt;SEP&gt;The ureters are tubes that carry urine from the kidneys to the bladder and can be examined during ureteroscopy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urinary Tract">
      <data key="d0">Urinary Tract</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The urinary tract includes the kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra, all working together to store and eliminate urine.&lt;SEP&gt;The urinary tract is the system of organs responsible for producing and eliminating urine, including the kidneys, ureters, and urethra.&lt;SEP&gt;The urinary tract includes the kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra, and is examined during various diagnostic procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Mutations">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Mutations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Genetic mutations are changes in DNA that can contribute to the development of leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic mutations are changes in DNA that can increase the risk of developing prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic mutations are changes in DNA that can lead to the development of cancerous cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Small Cell Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Small Cell Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Small cell carcinoma is a rare and aggressive type of bladder cancer that grows quickly and spreads easily.&lt;SEP&gt;Small cell carcinoma is a rare and aggressive type of non-urothelial bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Telehealth Visits">
      <data key="d0">Telehealth Visits</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Telehealth visits are remote medical consultations conducted through digital communication platforms.&lt;SEP&gt;Telehealth visits are remote medical consultations that allow patients to connect with their healthcare providers via phone or video call.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contact Information">
      <data key="d0">Contact Information</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Contact information includes details such as names, phone numbers, and addresses of individuals involved in a patient's care.&lt;SEP&gt;Contact information includes details such as phone numbers and email addresses of a patient's care team members.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Emergency Communication">
      <data key="d0">Emergency Communication</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Emergency communication refers to the methods used to contact a healthcare provider in urgent situations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blood Test">
      <data key="d0">Blood Test</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood Test is a medical procedure that involves drawing blood to analyze for signs of disease, conditions, or health status. It is a diagnostic tool used to detect genetic changes in leukemia cells and to confirm the diagnosis of chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) by analyzing blood samples. Blood tests are also employed to assess organ function and gather information about a patient's overall health as part of the diagnostic process for various conditions, including cutaneous B-cell lymphoma. The procedure typically involves taking a sample of blood, which is then analyzed in a laboratory to identify abnormalities or indicators of illness. Blood tests serve a broad range of purposes in medical diagnostics, from monitoring health to detecting specific diseases. They are widely used in clinical settings to support diagnosis, treatment planning, and health management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68217ea9e5382d1756c99b5152ea98db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tumor Staging">
      <data key="d0">Tumor Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tumor staging is a method used by cancer experts to describe the extent of cancer in the body based on tumor size, lymph node involvement, and metastasis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839709</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T4">
      <data key="d0">T4</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">T4 is a classification in the TNM system indicating that the tumor has grown outside the prostate gland.&lt;SEP&gt;T4 indicates a tumor of any size that has invaded nearby structures such as the chest wall or skin.&lt;SEP&gt;T4 indicates a tumor spanning 3 pelvic segments or crossing the sacroiliac joint (SIJ).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839709</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="N1">
      <data key="d0">N1</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">N1 is a classification in the TNM system indicating that cancer has spread to nearby lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;N1 indicates cancer found in regional lymph nodes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839709</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="M1">
      <data key="d0">M1</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">M1 is a classification in the TNM system indicating that cancer has spread to distant parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;M1 indicates distant metastasis is found.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839709</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PSA">
      <data key="d0">PSA</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">PSA (prostate-specific antigen) is a protein produced by the prostate gland that helps nourish and transmit semen.&lt;SEP&gt;PSA stands for Prostate-Specific Antigen, a protein produced by the prostate that can be measured in blood to help detect prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;PSA (Prostate-Specific Antigen) is a protein produced by the prostate, with elevated levels indicating possible prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;PSA is a blood test that measures prostate-specific antigen levels, which may indicate prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;PSA is a protein produced by the prostate that can be measured in the blood to detect potential prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839709</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gleason Score">
      <data key="d0">Gleason Score</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Gleason score is a system used to evaluate the aggressiveness of prostate cancer based on the appearance of cancer cells under a microscope.&lt;SEP&gt;Gleason Score is a grading system used to evaluate the aggressiveness of prostate cancer based on biopsy samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Gleason score is a grading system used to assess the aggressiveness of prostate cancer based on tissue samples.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839709</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Test">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Test</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A genetic test is a procedure used to identify mutations in genes that may increase cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;A genetic test is a medical procedure used to identify harmful changes in genes that may increase the risk of developing diseases such as cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A genetic test is used to identify abnormal changes in genes that may increase cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839709</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Cells">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer cells are abnormal cells that grow and divide uncontrollably. This uncontrolled growth can lead to the formation of tumors, which may spread to other parts of the body through the blood or lymphatic system. Cancer cells have the potential to metastasize, meaning they can travel to distant locations and form new tumors. These cells often appear brighter in imaging scans, such as PET scans, and can be identified through microscopic examination. The ability of cancer cells to grow and spread uncontrollably is a defining characteristic of cancer, distinguishing them from normal cells. They may also be detected using various imaging procedures, depending on the type and location of the cancer. Overall, cancer cells represent a significant health concern due to their aggressive behavior and potential to affect multiple organs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf2d987135a5936876bc819136e3a5b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d1ec9b874dd38ef0f3a4a2081f548e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839709</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inherited Genetic Mutation">
      <data key="d0">Inherited Genetic Mutation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An inherited genetic mutation occurs in every cell in the body and can increase the risk of developing cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839710</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Somatic Mutation">
      <data key="d0">Somatic Mutation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A somatic mutation is a genetic change that occurs in some cells of the body, not inherited.&lt;SEP&gt;A somatic mutation is a genetic change that occurs in non-reproductive cells and is not passed to offspring.&lt;SEP&gt;A somatic mutation occurs only in the cells of a tumor and is not inherited.&lt;SEP&gt;A somatic mutation is a genetic change that occurs in non-reproductive cells and is not inherited.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839710</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hormone Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Hormone Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Hormone therapy is a treatment for prostate cancer that reduces the levels of hormones that promote cancer growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone Therapy is a treatment option for advanced-stage prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone therapy is a treatment for prostate cancer that aims to block testosterone production or activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone therapy is a treatment that blocks hormones from helping cancer cells grow.&lt;SEP&gt;Hormone therapy is a treatment that adds, blocks, or removes hormones to treat cancer, particularly prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839710</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Hormone Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Non-Hormone Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-hormone therapy refers to treatments for cancer that do not involve hormonal manipulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839710</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ADT">
      <data key="d0">ADT</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">ADT stands for Androgen Deprivation Therapy, a type of hormone therapy that reduces testosterone levels to slow cancer growth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839710</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Androgen Deprivation Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Androgen Deprivation Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Androgen Deprivation Therapy is a treatment that lowers testosterone levels to a very low level, used in prostate cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Androgen Deprivation Therapy (ADT) is a treatment that lowers testosterone levels to reduce the growth of prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839710</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prostate">
      <data key="d0">Prostate</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The prostate is a gland in the male reproductive system that produces seminal fluid and contains muscles involved in ejaculation. It is a small gland located in the pelvis, below the bladder, and surrounds the urethra just beneath the bladder. The prostate plays a key role in the male reproductive system by contributing to the production of semen. It can be affected by various conditions, including cancer, enlargement, and other diseases. Prostate cancer is one of the most common cancers among men, and the prostate is often the focus of medical evaluations, including imaging tests and biopsies for cancer detection. The gland's function and health are important aspects of male reproductive and urinary health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839710</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Physical Exam">
      <data key="d0">Physical Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Physical Exam is a medical assessment conducted by a healthcare provider to evaluate a patient's overall health. It involves examining the patient's body for signs of illness, disease, or abnormalities. The process typically includes checking vital signs, conducting a head and neck examination, and inspecting and palpating various body parts to assess health conditions. A physical exam is also used to detect abnormalities, including in specific areas such as the breast, and to identify any signs of illness or disease.  

The primary purpose of a physical exam is to evaluate overall health, monitor health status, and detect changes that may indicate underlying medical issues. It is a clinical assessment performed by a healthcare provider, often involving a thorough check of the body to identify potential health concerns. In some cases, it may be conducted by a team member, though it is most commonly carried out by a qualified medical professional.  

Additionally, a physical exam is used to assess the presence of cancer symptoms and to determine the patient's condition. It serves as an essential tool in diagnosing and managing health problems, providing valuable information that guides further medical decisions. The procedure is designed to evaluate the patient's body systematically and objectively, ensuring a comprehensive understanding of their current health status.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f9a9eb8b01f29fdf214c10bdffac3203&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8eae4d6dadf6a6fbd339efa4dec2172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839710</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LHRH Agonist">
      <data key="d0">LHRH Agonist</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">LHRH Agonist is a type of hormone therapy that stimulates the release of luteinizing hormone, leading to reduced testosterone production.&lt;SEP&gt;LHRH agonists are medications used in ADT to lower testosterone production.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Goserelin">
      <data key="d0">Goserelin</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Goserelin is a specific LHRH agonist used in androgen deprivation therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Goserelin is a medication used in ADT to reduce testosterone levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Goserelin is a drug used in ovarian suppression, also known as Zoladex.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Leuprolide">
      <data key="d0">Leuprolide</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Leuprolide is a commonly used LHRH agonist in hormone therapy for prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Leuprolide is a medication used in ADT to lower testosterone production.&lt;SEP&gt;Leuprolide is a drug used in ovarian suppression, also known as Lupron Depot.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Triptorelin">
      <data key="d0">Triptorelin</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Triptorelin is an LHRH agonist used in androgen deprivation therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Triptorelin is a medication used in ADT to decrease testosterone levels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nilutamide">
      <data key="d0">Nilutamide</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Nilutamide is a medication used as an anti-androgen in hormone therapy for prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Nilutamide is a medication used in ADT to block testosterone from affecting cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Flutamide">
      <data key="d0">Flutamide</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Flutamide is an anti-androgen used in combination with LHRH agonists to treat prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Flutamide is a medication used in ADT to block the effects of testosterone on cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bicalutamide">
      <data key="d0">Bicalutamide</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Bicalutamide is an anti-androgen used in hormone therapy for prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Bicalutamide is a medication used in ADT to prevent testosterone from binding to cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Degarelix">
      <data key="d0">Degarelix</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Degarelix is an LHRH antagonist used in androgen deprivation therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Degarelix is a medication used in ADT to block testosterone production.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Relugolix">
      <data key="d0">Relugolix</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Relugolix is an LHRH antagonist available as a daily tablet for hormone therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Relugolix is a medication used in ADT to lower testosterone levels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Orchiectomy">
      <data key="d0">Orchiectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Orchiectomy is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of one or both testicles to reduce testosterone production.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Testosterone">
      <data key="d0">Testosterone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Testosterone is a hormone primarily produced in the testes, responsible for male sexual characteristics and reproductive functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Testosterone is a male hormone that plays a role in the growth of prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Testosterone is a hormone produced by the adrenal glands, testicles, and ovaries, and it may be suppressed in endocrine therapy for males.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Androgens">
      <data key="d0">Androgens</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Androgens are male hormones, including testosterone, that can promote the growth of prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Patient Guides for Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Patient Guides for Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Patient Guides for Cancer are educational resources offering information on cancer treatment and management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Imaging Scans">
      <data key="d0">Imaging Scans</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Imaging scans are used to assess whether cancer has spread deeper into the skin or to other parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging scans are medical procedures used to create images of the inside of the body for diagnostic purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging scans are used to visualize internal body structures and detect potential tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839712</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Biopsies">
      <data key="d0">Biopsies</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Biopsies are medical procedures where tissue samples are taken for examination to confirm the presence of cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Biopsies are medical procedures used to remove tissue samples for examination under a microscope.&lt;SEP&gt;Biopsies are medical procedures where a small sample of tissue is taken for examination.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
