    <node id="Treatment Options">
      <data key="d0">Treatment Options</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Treatment Options refer to the various approaches available for treating cancer, including standard treatments and clinical trials. These options encompass a range of medical interventions designed to manage or cure the disease, such as surgery, radiation, chemotherapy, and other therapies. Treatment options are determined based on a patient's risk group, with lower-risk patients receiving minimal or no treatment and higher-risk patients receiving more aggressive treatment. They include preferred therapies, other recommended therapies, and case-specific therapies. In the context of bladder cancer, treatment options may include surgery, intravesical therapy, systemic therapy, radiation therapy, clinical trials, and supportive care. Overall, treatment options are the various medical approaches available to manage a disease, incorporating both established methods and emerging therapeutic strategies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839714</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bronchioles">
      <data key="d0">Bronchioles</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Bronchioles are small airways in the lungs that branch from the bronchus and lead to the alveoli.&lt;SEP&gt;Bronchioles are small airways branching from the bronchi, leading to the alveoli.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839714</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Alveoli">
      <data key="d0">Alveoli</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Alveoli are small sacs in the lungs where oxygen is transferred into the bloodstream.&lt;SEP&gt;The Alveoli are small sacs at the end of the bronchioli where oxygen is transferred into the blood.&lt;SEP&gt;Alveoli are tiny air sacs in the lungs where gas exchange occurs between the air and the bloodstream.&lt;SEP&gt;Alveoli are small air sacs in the lungs where oxygen is transferred into the blood.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839714</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Screening">
      <data key="d0">Screening</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Screening is a process used to detect lung cancer at an early stage, before symptoms appear, to improve treatment outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Screening is the process of checking for diseases in people without symptoms to detect them early.&lt;SEP&gt;Screening is the process of checking for diseases, such as breast cancer, before symptoms appear.&lt;SEP&gt;Screening is the process of testing for diseases in people without symptoms to detect them early.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4bc8b1b941d18ac455e5f255e1df8c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e75e869fcfcb7c5431dbcdd532137f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839714</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Second-Hand Smoke">
      <data key="d0">Second-Hand Smoke</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Second-hand smoke is the smoke inhaled by non-smokers from the exhalation of smokers and combustion of tobacco products.&lt;SEP&gt;Second-Hand Smoke is the smoke exhaled by smokers and from burning tobacco products, increasing lung cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Second-hand smoke refers to the inhalation of tobacco smoke from others, increasing the risk of lung cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-08475506372bb4ce9ec1bd326caf0fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839714</data>
