    <node id="Chronic Myeloid Leukemia">
      <data key="d0">Chronic Myeloid Leukemia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) is a type of blood cancer caused by the Philadelphia chromosome and the BCR::ABL1 gene.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic myeloid leukemia (CML) is a type of blood cancer characterized by an abnormal gene fusion.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic myeloid leukemia (CML) is a type of blood cancer characterized by the overproduction of myeloid cells, often caused by the BCR::ABL1 gene.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839716</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BCR::ABL1">
      <data key="d0">BCR::ABL1</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">BCR::ABL1 is a fused gene resulting from a chromosomal translocation in CML.&lt;SEP&gt;BCR::ABL1 is a fused gene formed by the exchange of genetic material between chromosome 9 and chromosome 22, which is associated with chronic myeloid leukemia (CML).&lt;SEP&gt;BCR::ABL1 is a genetic mutation that leads to the production of the BCR::ABL protein, which drives the growth of certain types of ALL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b11b0c66441242d2f687a0c55adee585</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839716</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Philadelphia Chromosome">
      <data key="d0">Philadelphia Chromosome</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Philadelphia chromosome is a shortened chromosome 22 formed by the fusion of parts of chromosomes 9 and 22, associated with Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML).&lt;SEP&gt;The Philadelphia chromosome is an abnormal chromosome resulting from the fusion of parts of chromosomes 9 and 22, characteristic of CML.&lt;SEP&gt;The Philadelphia chromosome is a shortened chromosome formed by a translocation between chromosomes 9 and 22 in CML.&lt;SEP&gt;The Philadelphia chromosome is a shortened version of chromosome 22 resulting from the exchange of genetic material with chromosome 9, and it is a hallmark of CML.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Differentiation">
      <data key="d0">Differentiation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Differentiation is the process by which blood stem cells develop into specialized blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Progenitor Cells">
      <data key="d0">Progenitor Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Progenitor cells are intermediate cells that develop into mature blood cells such as red blood cells, white blood cells, and platelets.&lt;SEP&gt;Progenitor cells are early-stage cells that develop into mature blood cells such as red blood cells, white blood cells, or platelets.&lt;SEP&gt;Progenitor cells are intermediate cells that develop into mature blood cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Granulocytes">
      <data key="d0">Granulocytes</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Granulocytes are a type of white blood cell that includes neutrophils, eosinophils, and basophils, involved in fighting infections.&lt;SEP&gt;Granulocytes are a type of white blood cell that includes neutrophils, eosinophils, and basophils.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd7ea43a74059d6781866faec437f19a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Neutrophils">
      <data key="d0">Neutrophils</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Neutrophils are a type of granulocyte that play a key role in the immune system by fighting bacterial infections.&lt;SEP&gt;Neutrophils are a type of white blood cell that defend the body against bacterial infections.&lt;SEP&gt;Neutrophils are a type of granulocyte that helps fight bacterial infections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Eosinophils">
      <data key="d0">Eosinophils</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Eosinophils are a type of granulocyte involved in combating parasitic infections and allergic reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Eosinophils are a type of granulocyte involved in fighting parasitic infections and allergic reactions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Basophils">
      <data key="d0">Basophils</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Basophils are a type of granulocyte that release histamine and other chemicals during allergic reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Basophils are a type of granulocyte involved in inflammatory responses and allergic reactions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CML">
      <data key="d0">CML</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">CML refers to Chronic Myeloid Leukemia, a type of blood cancer characterized by an overproduction of white blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;CML is a type of leukemia characterized by an overproduction of myeloid cells and the presence of the Philadelphia chromosome.&lt;SEP&gt;CML is a type of blood cancer caused by a specific genetic mutation involving the BCR::ABL1 gene.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef6586b896c47b361bf4f6aabb4c35d5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Guide">
      <data key="d0">Guide</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Guide provides information on follow-up exam schedules for different types of squamous cell skin cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A guide is a resource that provides information on possible tests and procedures related to AML.&lt;SEP&gt;A guide is a resource providing information on cancer care and treatment options.&lt;SEP&gt;Guide refers to a document or resource that lists targeted therapies for metastatic cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b66e38931f28ed6ac9b231faaf202fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Book">
      <data key="d0">Book</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A book is a written or printed work containing information on cancer care and treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The book provides information on bone cancer, its diagnosis, treatment, and patient care.&lt;SEP&gt;A book is a written work that provides information and guidance, in this case, about gliomas and their treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nerves">
      <data key="d0">Nerves</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Nerves are part of the body's nervous system and can be affected by certain conditions, causing symptoms such as pain, burning, or loss of feeling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839717</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pain">
      <data key="d0">Pain</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Pain is a common symptom associated with nerve involvement and other medical conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Pain is a common side effect of a biopsy, often managed with anesthesia.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical discomfort that may persist after cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Burning">
      <data key="d0">Burning</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Burning is a type of sensory symptom that may occur due to nerve damage or other medical issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stinging">
      <data key="d0">Stinging</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stinging is a sharp, painful sensation that can result from nerve irritation or injury.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Brain">
      <data key="d0">Brain</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The brain is the central organ of the central nervous system, responsible for controlling bodily functions and serving as the primary site for various neurological processes. It is also the central organ of the nervous system, where gliomas commonly originate and cause symptoms by pressing on or invading brain tissue. The brain is a critical organ in the central nervous system where primary CNS lymphoma may develop, and it is affected by primary CNS lymphoma. Additionally, the brain is a common site for breast cancer metastasis. In medical contexts, the brain may refer to the injection site for intrathecal chemotherapy. The brain is a vital organ that can show up as a bright spot on PET scans due to its high metabolic activity. Furthermore, the brain is a part of the body that may be examined for signs of leukemia.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06f823f3a91fcbc32c62fac3c6347715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Loss of Feeling">
      <data key="d0">Loss of Feeling</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Loss of feeling refers to the inability to sense touch, temperature, or other stimuli, often caused by nerve damage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Double or Blurred Vision">
      <data key="d0">Double or Blurred Vision</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Double or blurred vision is a visual impairment that may indicate underlying neurological or medical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Skin Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A skin biopsy is a procedure where a sample of skin tissue is removed and examined under a microscope to diagnose skin cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;A skin biopsy involves removing a sample of tissue for testing to determine if cancer is present.&lt;SEP&gt;A skin biopsy is a diagnostic procedure involving the removal of a small tissue sample for examination under a microscope.&lt;SEP&gt;Skin Biopsy is a procedure where a sample of inflamed skin on the breast is removed to diagnose inflammatory breast cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Skin Biopsy is a procedure that takes a small sample of inflamed skin on the breast.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ac9bf8f198bc5ad54fd1a7b843e810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Connective Tissue">
      <data key="d0">Connective Tissue</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Connective tissue is a type of tissue that provides support and structure to the body, and its presence in tumors can indicate high-risk cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Connective tissue provides structural support and helps maintain the shape of the breast.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tumor Depth">
      <data key="d0">Tumor Depth</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tumor depth refers to how deeply a tumor has invaded into the skin, which affects the risk of recurrence or spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blood Vessels">
      <data key="d0">Blood Vessels</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood vessels are channels that carry blood throughout the body and can be involved in the spread of cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood vessels are the network of tubes that transport blood throughout the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood vessels are part of the circulatory system and can carry cancer cells to other parts of the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood vessels are networks of tubes that transport blood throughout the breast.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a93aa507dd7d98a02e8ba92d39e3649&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lymphovascular Invasion">
      <data key="d0">Lymphovascular Invasion</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Lymphovascular invasion refers to the presence of cancer cells in lymph or blood vessels outside the main tumor, indicating a higher risk of spreading.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Weakened Immune System">
      <data key="d0">Weakened Immune System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A weakened immune system increases the risk of squamous cell skin cancer, especially after organ transplantation or in cases of certain diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakened immune system is a condition where the body's defense mechanisms are compromised, increasing the risk of infections and cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Human Immunodeficiency Virus">
      <data key="d0">Human Immunodeficiency Virus</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a viral infection that weakens the immune system, increasing the risk of skin cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a virus that weakens the immune system and can lead to acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS).&lt;SEP&gt;Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) is a virus that can lead to acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS) and requires specialized treatment in patients with primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Human immunodeficiency virus is a virus that can lead to acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS) and may influence cancer treatment options.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV is a virus that weakens the immune system, increasing the risk of HPV infection and related cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="AIDS">
      <data key="d0">AIDS</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
      <data key="d2">AIDS is the final stage of HIV infection, characterized by severe immune system damage.&lt;SEP&gt;AIDS is the final stage of HIV infection, significantly weakening the immune system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Organ Transplant">
      <data key="d0">Organ Transplant</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">An organ transplant is a medical procedure where an organ is transferred from one person to another, which can weaken the immune system.&lt;SEP&gt;An organ transplant involves replacing a failing organ with a healthy one, often requiring immunosuppressive medications.&lt;SEP&gt;Organ transplant involves receiving an organ from another person, often requiring immunosuppressant medications that can increase cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CSCC">
      <data key="d0">CSCC</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
      <data key="d2">CSCC is an abbreviation for squamous cell skin cancer, a type of cancer that affects the outer layer of the skin.&lt;SEP&gt;CSCC stands for Cutaneous Squamous Cell Carcinoma, a type of skin cancer that can be classified as local, regional, or metastatic based on its spread.&lt;SEP&gt;CSCC stands for Cutaneous Squamous Cell Carcinoma, a type of skin cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;CSCC stands for Cutaneous Squamous Cell Carcinoma, a common type of skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Shave Excision">
      <data key="d0">Shave Excision</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Shave excision is a procedure where a thin layer of skin is removed to treat early-stage skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mohs Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Mohs Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Mohs surgery is a specialized procedure used to remove cancer while preserving healthy tissue.&lt;SEP&gt;Mohs surgery is a specialized surgical technique used to remove skin cancers, particularly for high-risk or very high-risk CSCC, with high cure rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Mohs surgery is a specialized technique used to remove skin cancer with high precision.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d994e430bb9890c905d7914fad9c118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839719</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="E-Cigarettes">
      <data key="d0">E-Cigarettes</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">E-cigarettes are electronic devices used to inhale vaporized nicotine, often associated with smoking cessation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839719</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Other Cancers">
      <data key="d0">Other Cancers</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
      <data key="d2">Other cancers are potential long-term side effects of systemic therapy, indicating an increased risk of developing additional malignancies.&lt;SEP&gt;Other cancers refer to additional types of cancer that may develop in individuals who have already had one type of cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Other cancers can be long-term side effects of chemotherapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839719</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="High-Risk">
      <data key="d0">High-Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">High-risk refers to a classification of cancer that is more likely to spread or recur after treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839719</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Very High-Risk">
      <data key="d0">Very High-Risk</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Very high-risk refers to a classification of cancer that poses a significant threat of spreading or recurring.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839719</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor">
      <data key="d0">Immune Checkpoint Inhibitor</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An immune checkpoint inhibitor is a type of drug that helps the immune system recognize and attack cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;An immune checkpoint inhibitor is a type of immunotherapy used to treat cancer by enhancing the immune system's response.&lt;SEP&gt;Immune checkpoint inhibitors are drugs that help the immune system fight cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;An immune checkpoint inhibitor is a type of immunotherapy that helps the immune system fight cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;An immune checkpoint inhibitor is a type of immunotherapy that may be used before surgery for some anal cancer patients.&lt;SEP&gt;An immune checkpoint inhibitor is a type of immunotherapy drug that helps the immune system recognize and attack cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839719</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wider Margin">
      <data key="d0">Wider Margin</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A wider margin refers to the amount of healthy tissue removed around a tumor during surgery to ensure complete cancer removal.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
