    <node id="Alkaline Phosphatase">
      <data key="d0">Alkaline Phosphatase</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme found in the blood, with elevated levels indicating possible cancer spread to the bone or liver.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkaline phosphatase (ALP) is an enzyme found in the blood, with elevated levels indicating possible bone tumors, liver disorders, or pregnancy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839720</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Liver Function Tests">
      <data key="d0">Liver Function Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Liver function tests are blood tests used to evaluate the health and function of the liver.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver Function Tests are blood tests that measure chemicals processed by the liver.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver function tests are blood tests that measure how well the liver is working.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver function tests measure substances in the blood to assess the health and function of the liver.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver function tests measure chemicals processed by the liver to determine its health.&lt;SEP&gt;Liver function tests measure enzymes produced by the liver to evaluate its health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e63736c94b8b08a565c3d8679d3b57</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839720</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Treatment">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Treatment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Cancer Treatment refers to a range of medical interventions used to eliminate or control cancer. These therapies include surgery, radiation, chemotherapy, immunotherapy, and other diagnostic and therapeutic procedures. The specific approach taken depends on factors such as tumor location, cancer stage, and the overall health of the patient. Cancer Treatment involves determining the best course of action tailored to individual cases, with the goal of managing and eliminating cancerous cells. In addition to addressing the disease itself, cancer treatment can have broader implications, such as impacting fertility. The process encompasses various methods aimed at treating cancer, with the ultimate objective of improving patient outcomes and quality of life.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33608457001e818e2b300adae9c6c0d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839721</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Contraception">
      <data key="d0">Contraception</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Contraception, such as condoms, is recommended to prevent pregnancy during and after cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Contraception refers to methods used to prevent pregnancy, including barrier methods and IUDs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839721</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Menstruation">
      <data key="d0">Menstruation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Menstruation is the monthly shedding of the uterine lining, influenced by hormonal changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Menstruation refers to the monthly shedding of the uterine lining, which may be affected by cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839721</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Birth Control">
      <data key="d0">Birth Control</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Birth Control refers to methods used to prevent pregnancy, especially important during cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Birth control refers to methods used to prevent pregnancy, including hormonal and non-hormonal options.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-052101b592e186cce702983d2acc67e4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
