      <data key="d5">1772839721</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Tests">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Genetic tests are used to identify hereditary conditions that may increase the risk of adrenal tumors.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic tests are used to identify specific gene mutations or abnormalities that may affect cancer treatment and prognosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic tests are used to identify specific genetic mutations or abnormalities that may be associated with a disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic tests are used to detect genes associated with hereditary conditions that increase the risk of pancreatic cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic tests are used to identify inherited mutations related to pancreatic cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic tests are diagnostic procedures used to analyze DNA for mutations or genetic markers associated with diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Tests analyzing DNA to identify genetic factors related to cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839722</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Binder">
      <data key="d0">Medical Binder</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Medical Binder is a tool used to organize medical records, test results, and other health-related documents or information in one place. It serves as a structured and centralized system for managing patient data, facilitating easy access and reference. Some descriptions specify that it is particularly useful for patients undergoing skin cancer diagnosis and treatment, highlighting its role in tracking specific types of medical information such as imaging reports, cancer reports, and treatment details. The term "notebook" is sometimes used to describe the physical or digital format of the binder, emphasizing its function as a portable and organized record-keeping device. Medical Binder is also described as a collection of medical records and documents designed for efficient management and accessibility. Overall, it is a critical resource for both healthcare providers and patients to maintain and retrieve important health information systematically.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0bd86bf8fc82f14fa5f7f51d924514e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7102a43dfb62e649d725bc95ba292688&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839722</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Biomarker Tests">
      <data key="d0">Biomarker Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Biomarker tests are used to detect specific markers in the body that can indicate the presence or progression of a disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomarker tests are used to detect specific biological markers that may indicate the presence or progression of a disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomarker tests are used to profile cancer characteristics and guide treatment strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Biomarker tests are used to profile pancreatic cancer for targeted treatment options.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6268b6efa690f6e094e443dca6b4cb52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97836a515d346931beb424ae40a89877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839722</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diagnostic Radiologist">
      <data key="d0">Diagnostic Radiologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A diagnostic radiologist is a specialist who interprets imaging scans for cancer diagnosis.&lt;SEP&gt;A diagnostic radiologist interprets imaging tests such as mammograms and ultrasounds.&lt;SEP&gt;A diagnostic radiologist interprets imaging tests such as x-rays to detect disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea00cf063e8831db4919330d94b1f2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839722</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Platinum-Based Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d0">Platinum-Based Chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Platinum-Based Chemotherapy is a type of cancer treatment that uses drugs containing platinum to kill cancer cells. It is categorized as a systemic therapy, meaning it works throughout the body to target cancer cells. The chemotherapy involves medications such as carboplatin, cisplatin, and oxaliplatin, which are commonly used in various cancer treatments.  

Platinum-Based Chemotherapy is a recommended treatment option when used with radiation therapy, particularly in cases of cutaneous squamous cell carcinoma (CSCC). It is also a preferred treatment approach in combination with radiation therapy. This treatment is widely used for ovarian cancer, where it is considered a standard option, often administered in both initial and recurrent settings. It is frequently combined with taxanes to enhance its effectiveness.  

Additionally, Platinum-Based Chemotherapy is a common systemic therapy for cervical cancer and is used in treating metastatic cervical cancer. It is also recognized as the first-line treatment for metastatic anal cancer. These applications highlight its versatility and importance in oncology across multiple cancer types.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839722</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Interventional Radiologist">
      <data key="d0">Interventional Radiologist</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An interventional radiologist performs minimally invasive procedures using imaging guidance for diagnosis or treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;An interventional radiologist performs minimally invasive procedures for cancer diagnosis and treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;An interventional radiologist performs procedures such as needle biopsies and places IV ports.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0fb70c1c798caae12ac2d64e61bcbad4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f</data>
