    <node id="HER2">
      <data key="d0">HER2</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">HER2 is a protein that plays a role in cell growth and is often overexpressed in certain cancers, particularly breast cancer. HER2 is a biomarker tested in breast cancer to determine if the cancer is likely to respond to specific treatments. The overexpression of HER2 can influence treatment decisions, as it indicates the presence of a protein that promotes cancer growth. In some cases, HER2 overexpression is associated with more aggressive forms of breast cancer, and it can affect the choice of therapies, such as targeted treatments. While HER2 is primarily linked to breast cancer, it is also involved in normal cell growth and can be present in some breast cancer cells. Additionally, the presence of HER2 may impact treatment options, as PARP inhibitors are not typically used when HER2 is overexpressed. Overall, HER2 is a key factor in the diagnosis and management of certain cancers, particularly breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-562e1870b5e20f8648a2e56d960a1148&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc469adbdd7a41816d59f249439bc726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
