    <node id="PET/CT Scan">
      <data key="d0">PET/CT Scan</data>
      <data key="d1">equipment</data>
      <data key="d2">PET/CT Scan is a combined imaging technique that merges positron emission tomography (PET) and computed tomography (CT) to provide detailed images of the body. This procedure integrates the functional data from PET scans with the anatomical details from CT scans, allowing for a comprehensive view of internal structures. A PET/CT scan is a medical imaging test that combines PET and CT to produce detailed cross-sectional views of the body. It is also described as a combined imaging procedure that uses both PET and CT scans to provide detailed views of the body's internal structures. The primary purpose of a PET/CT scan is to detect cancer cells throughout the body, including cases where cancer has spread beyond the bladder. Additionally, it is used to detect cancer by combining positron emission tomography with computed tomography, offering a powerful tool for diagnosing and staging various types of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-27b3a0f53b4be1d525497f87555d7a06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
