    <node id="Eligibility Criteria">
      <data key="d0">Eligibility Criteria</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Eligibility criteria are rules that determine who can participate in a clinical trial, based on factors such as age, cancer stage, and health status.&lt;SEP&gt;Eligibility criteria are the rules that determine who can participate in a clinical trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Eligibility criteria are rules that determine who can join a clinical trial.&lt;SEP&gt;Eligibility criteria are rules that determine who can participate in a clinical trial, based on factors like age, cancer type, and health status.&lt;SEP&gt;Eligibility criteria are rules that determine who can participate in a clinical trial, based on factors like age, cancer type, and treatment history.&lt;SEP&gt;Eligibility criteria are rules that determine who can participate in a clinical trial based on factors like age, cancer stage, and health status.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48b513355d29308e212a3074ba326b10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839728</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Informed Consent">
      <data key="d0">Informed Consent</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Informed consent is a process where participants are provided detailed information about a clinical trial's purpose, risks, and benefits before agreeing to participate.&lt;SEP&gt;Informed consent is the process of providing detailed information about a clinical trial before participation.&lt;SEP&gt;Informed consent is a process where participants are provided with detailed information about a clinical trial before agreeing to participate.&lt;SEP&gt;Informed consent is a process where participants are fully informed about a clinical trial's purpose, risks, and benefits before agreeing to participate.&lt;SEP&gt;Informed consent is a process in which participants in a clinical trial are fully informed about the study's purpose, risks, and benefits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-541f1323a24c5990b4a6408e0c5442ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551</data>
