    <node id="MRI Scan">
      <data key="d0">MRI Scan</data>
      <data key="d1">equipment</data>
      <data key="d2">MRI Scan is a medical imaging technique that uses radio waves and powerful magnets to produce detailed images of the body's internal structures. It is widely used in medical diagnostics for visualizing soft tissues, organs, and other internal features. The process involves applying magnetic fields and radio waves to generate high-resolution images without the use of ionizing radiation. MRI scans are commonly employed to detect a variety of conditions, including prostate issues, where they help assess the size of the prostate and aid in calculating PSA density. Additionally, MRI scans are particularly useful in identifying prostate cancer and detecting lymphoma in the central nervous system. The technique is also referred to as a medical imaging procedure or test, and it creates detailed images of the body's internal structures by utilizing magnetic fields and radio waves.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aa14ecd19e2d721cb99ea9590f0ede3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705ff2bd04b2b58b98187f60f23a659e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
