    <node id="Abdominoperineal Resection">
      <data key="d0">Abdominoperineal Resection</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Abdominoperineal resection is a type of transabdominal surgery for tumors in the lower rectum, often requiring a permanent colostomy.&lt;SEP&gt;Abdominoperineal resection (APR) is a surgical procedure to remove the anus and surrounding tissue for recurrent or progressive anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Abdominoperineal resection is a surgical procedure to remove cancer from the anal area, often involving colostomy.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical procedure involving removal of the anus, rectum, and nearby tissues, requiring a permanent colostomy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
