    <node id="Colostomy">
      <data key="d0">Colostomy</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A colostomy is a surgical opening created to allow stool to exit the body, either temporarily or permanently.&lt;SEP&gt;A colostomy is a surgical procedure that connects a part of the colon to the outside of the abdomen to divert stool.&lt;SEP&gt;A colostomy is a surgical procedure that creates an opening in the colon to allow stool to exit the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A colostomy is a surgical opening created to allow stool to exit the body through the abdomen after abdominoperineal resection.&lt;SEP&gt;A colostomy is a surgical opening created in the colon to allow waste to exit the body, often performed after APR surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;A colostomy is a surgical procedure creating an opening in the colon to allow waste to exit the body, often used after certain types of surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;A surgical procedure creating an opening in the abdomen for waste elimination after the anus is removed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cfcc365cd093374564eb27dcbf5b82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-419f40f64b13b1b2d0fac3cfb9fde92a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839734</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Groin">
      <data key="d0">Groin</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Groin is a body region located at the lower part of the abdomen, near the thigh, where lymph nodes may be felt.&lt;SEP&gt;The area of the body where the thigh meets the abdomen.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67e9c4dc95841db7d0af39e1267ae71b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839734</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Human Papillomavirus">
      <data key="d0">Human Papillomavirus</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Human Papillomavirus (HPV) is a group of viruses that can cause abnormal tissue growth and certain types of cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Human Papillomavirus (HPV) is a group of viruses that can cause warts and certain types of cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Human papillomavirus is a sexually transmitted infection that is the primary cause of cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Human Papillomavirus is a virus that causes various types of cancers, including cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Human papillomavirus (HPV) is a group of viruses that can cause various cancers, including anal cancer, and has over 100 strains.&lt;SEP&gt;A virus that can cause abnormal tissue growth and is almost always responsible for anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d249262ff9e7e657de99a30199159cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839734</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Infertility">
      <data key="d0">Infertility</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Infertility is a potential long-term side effect of systemic therapy, indicating the loss of reproductive capability.&lt;SEP&gt;Infertility can be a long-term side effect of chemotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Infertility is the inability to produce children, which can result from cancer treatments like radiation or chemotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;The inability to produce children.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839735</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inguinal Lymph Nodes">
      <data key="d0">Inguinal Lymph Nodes</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Inguinal lymph nodes are located in the groin area and can be affected by anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Inguinal lymph nodes are located in the groin and may be affected by anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Lymph nodes located in the groin area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
