    <node id="Carcinoembryonic Antigen">
      <data key="d0">Carcinoembryonic Antigen</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Carcinoembryonic antigen (CEA) is a tumor marker often used in the monitoring of certain cancers, including breast cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Carcinoembryonic antigen is a protein that may be elevated in certain cancers, including colon cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee254e84e63bd35682ed56c41cef9247</data>
