      <data key="d0">CA 15-3</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">CA 15-3 is a tumor marker used to monitor the progression of breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839735</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tumor Mutational Burden">
      <data key="d0">Tumor Mutational Burden</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tumor mutational burden is the total number of mutations found in the DNA of a tumor, which can affect immunotherapy response.&lt;SEP&gt;Tumor mutational burden (TMB) is a measure of genetic mutations in a tumor, which can influence treatment options.&lt;SEP&gt;Tumor mutational burden refers to the number of mutations present in a tumor's DNA, with high mutational burden indicating more genetic changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Tumor mutational burden refers to the number of mutations present in a tumor's DNA, which can influence treatment response.&lt;SEP&gt;Tumor mutational burden refers to the number of mutations present in a tumor's DNA, which can influence treatment options.&lt;SEP&gt;Tumor mutational burden refers to the number of genetic mutations in a tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;Tumor mutational burden refers to the number of mutations present in a tumor's DNA.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839735</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TMB-H">
      <data key="d0">TMB-H</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">TMB-H stands for tumor mutational burden-high, indicating a high number of mutations in a tumor's DNA, often associated with better responses to immunotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;TMB-H stands for tumor mutational burden-high, which is defined as having 10 or more mutations per million base pairs of tumor DNA.&lt;SEP&gt;TMB-H stands for tumor mutational burden-high, indicating a high number of mutations in a tumor's DNA.&lt;SEP&gt;TMB-H refers to tumor mutational burden-high, a condition where there are 10 or more mutations per million base pairs of tumor DNA.&lt;SEP&gt;TMB-H stands for tumor mutational burden-high, indicating a high number of mutations in tumor DNA.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839735</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PD-1">
      <data key="d0">PD-1</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">PD-1 is a protein on the surface of T-cells that plays a role in regulating the immune response.&lt;SEP&gt;PD-1 is a protein on immune cells that can be targeted by checkpoint inhibitors to enhance the immune response against cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;PD-1 is a protein on immune cells that acts as an "off switch," which tumors exploit to avoid destruction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839735</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PD-L1">
      <data key="d0">PD-L1</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">PD-L1 is a protein found on some cancer cells that can prevent the immune system from attacking them, making it a target for immunotherapy.&lt;SEP&gt;PD-L1 is an immune protein that can suppress the immune response against cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;PD-L1 is a protein that can be found on the surface of some cancer cells and helps them evade the immune system.&lt;SEP&gt;PD-L1 is a protein found on cancer cells that can inhibit the immune system's ability to attack them.&lt;SEP&gt;PD-L1 is a protein found on the surface of some cancer cells that can suppress the immune response against the cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839735</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="FISH">
      <data key="d0">FISH</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) is a laboratory technique used to detect genetic abnormalities in cells.&lt;SEP&gt;FISH stands for Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization, a laboratory technique used to detect genetic abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839735</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PCR">
      <data key="d0">PCR</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is a laboratory technique used to amplify DNA segments for analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;PCR stands for polymerase chain reaction, a method used to replicate genetic material.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4724f6acaaa7931560b29614efc2927f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839735</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Risk Testing">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Risk Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Genetic risk testing identifies genetic factors that may increase the risk of developing esophageal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic risk testing assesses an individual's genetic predisposition to certain diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic risk testing is a process to identify genetic factors that may increase the risk of developing certain diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic risk testing identifies genetic mutations that may increase the risk of developing certain diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic risk testing assesses inherited genetic mutations that may increase the risk of developing certain diseases.&lt;SEP&gt;Genetic risk testing assesses an individual's likelihood of developing cancer based on genetic factors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c77e0d4642a374a51f87e7e25b19281f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839735</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BRCA Tests">
      <data key="d0">BRCA Tests</data>
      <data key="d1">test</data>
      <data key="d2">BRCA tests are used to identify mutations in the BRCA1 and BRCA2 genes, which are linked to increased cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839736</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Family Cancer Health History">
      <data key="d0">Family Cancer Health History</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Family cancer health history refers to the pattern of cancer diagnoses within a family, which can help assess genetic risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-650982a589c2d527bc13923ccd0569ef</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
