    <node id="Esophageal Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Esophageal Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Esophageal cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the esophagus.&lt;SEP&gt;Esophageal cancer starts when cells in the esophagus grow out of control, with two main types: squamous cell carcinoma and adenocarcinoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Esophageal Cancer is a type of cancer that can show p16 overexpression and is associated with HPV-related changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Esophageal cancer is a type of cancer that starts in the esophagus or at the junction between the esophagus and stomach.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839737</data>
