    <node id="Spleen">
      <data key="d0">Spleen</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The spleen is an organ in the lymphatic system that filters blood and plays a role in immune responses. It is also described as the largest organ of the lymphatic system, involved in blood filtration and storage. Additionally, the spleen is an organ that filters lymph fluid and removes foreign material, and it helps fight infections by filtering blood and participating in immune processes. The spleen may be affected by various diseases, including esophageal cancer, advanced ovarian cancer (specifically stage 4B), and leukemia. These descriptions highlight the spleen's critical functions in both the lymphatic and circulatory systems, as well as its potential involvement in pathological conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-01c80b2d18abb91c5be598d33cf7a33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb36cedd3f66584d65304e58b668eeab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db4e8318949a3fda5683c53985c6af05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839739</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adrenocortical Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Adrenocortical Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
