    </node>
    <node id="Transrectal Ultrasound">
      <data key="d0">Transrectal Ultrasound</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Transrectal ultrasound is a medical imaging technique used to measure the size of the prostate, which helps in calculating PSA density.&lt;SEP&gt;Transrectal ultrasound is a procedure where an ultrasound probe is inserted into the rectum to guide a prostate biopsy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-975e540ddee1810d43caf8df4adcf205</data>
