      <data key="d5">1772839741</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Age">
      <data key="d0">Age</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Age is a risk factor for basal cell skin cancer, with risk increasing as a person gets older due to cumulative sun exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;Age is the biggest risk factor for prostate cancer, with most cases occurring in individuals aged 65 and older.&lt;SEP&gt;Age is the biggest risk factor for prostate cancer, with the likelihood of developing it increasing as a person ages.&lt;SEP&gt;Age is a factor that influences PSA levels, with higher levels typically observed in older individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Age is a significant risk factor for prostate cancer, with higher incidence in older individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Age is a risk factor for bladder cancer, with the risk increasing as a person gets older.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839741</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Race">
      <data key="d0">Race</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Race influences the likelihood of developing prostate cancer, with Black males being at higher risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Race is a factor that affects PSA levels, with Black males generally having higher normal PSA levels than white males.&lt;SEP&gt;Race refers to differences in prostate cancer incidence and outcomes among different racial groups.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839741</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Enlarged Prostate">
      <data key="d0">Enlarged Prostate</data>
      <data key="d1">condition</data>
      <data key="d2">An enlarged prostate is a condition that can increase PSA levels and may be caused by factors other than cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839741</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sex">
      <data key="d0">Sex</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Sex is a factor that can temporarily increase PSA levels, particularly after ejaculation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839741</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fine-Needle Aspiration">
      <data key="d0">Fine-Needle Aspiration</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Fine-Needle Aspiration is a medical procedure that involves using a thin needle to extract cells or fluid from a lump, mass, or suspicious nodule for diagnostic purposes. It is a type of biopsy that uses a thin needle to remove a small sample of tissue or collect cells from a tumor or lymph node. Fine-Needle Aspiration is also described as a minimally invasive biopsy technique that allows for the analysis of cells or fluid obtained from areas of concern. The procedure is commonly used in cases such as CSCC (Cutaneous Squamous Cell Carcinoma) to gather samples for further examination. Fine-Needle Aspiration (FNA) is a biopsy technique that uses a needle to collect tissue samples, often employed to test lymph nodes or other abnormal growths. Overall, Fine-Needle Aspiration serves as an essential tool in diagnosing various conditions by providing cellular or fluid samples for laboratory analysis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839741</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Drugs and Supplements">
      <data key="d0">Drugs and Supplements</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Certain drugs and supplements can affect PSA levels, influencing the accuracy of test results.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839741</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Research">
      <data key="d0">Research</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Research plays a crucial role in improving cancer treatment and patient outcomes, leading to better and longer lives for those living with cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d61a5e7031ea811cc4dcc55a0a0e8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839741</data>
