    <node id="Radiation">
      <data key="d0">Radiation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Radiation is energy that travels through space in the form of waves or particles. It is a broad category of energy that includes both ionizing and non-ionizing forms, with applications across various fields. Radiation is a form of energy used in medical imaging and treatment, often in small amounts for diagnostic purposes. It is utilized in imaging procedures such as panoramic dental x-rays, PET scans, and CT scans, where it helps visualize internal structures of the body. In therapeutic contexts, radiation is a treatment method used to kill cancer cells and is often part of additional therapy for conditions like high-grade gliomas. Radiation therapy involves exposure to ionizing energy, which is specifically used in cancer therapy to destroy malignant cells. Additionally, radiation is a form of energy used in radiation therapy to kill cancer cells, highlighting its dual role in both diagnosis and treatment. Overall, radiation is a form of energy used in diagnostic and therapeutic procedures, such as CT scans, and refers to the use of x-rays or other energy sources in medical imaging. Its application spans from imaging to targeted cancer treatment, making it a critical component of modern medicine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ae40f53e9d867c255e1e6901f5cfb058&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76a038845aaedb9ef7852018f26778b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67015f3916810c4378b2ed269cc27f29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-594536d6aaa61f8f1699ba50bf218a33</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839743</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Asbestos">
      <data key="d0">Asbestos</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Asbestos is a mineral fiber that, when inhaled, increases the risk of lung cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Asbestos is a mineral fiber that, when inhaled, can lead to lung cancer and other respiratory diseases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
