    <node id="Epithelium">
      <data key="d0">Epithelium</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Epithelium is the innermost lining of the mucosa, composed of flat, thin cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Epithelium is the surface layer of the oral mucosa, composed of stratified squamous cells.&lt;SEP&gt;The epithelium is the surface layer of tissue surrounding the ovaries where most ovarian cancers originate.&lt;SEP&gt;The epithelium is the surface layer of tissue surrounding the ovaries and is a common site for ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ecc6c4bcd3cab65fa05ab5f3c55e528d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43f96815f23658d5b24fe95ed4bd5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4da30dee72e228147daa825e4f5be72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53afdc6713818c4177b64a712ecce11b</data>
