    <node id="Tracer">
      <data key="d0">Tracer</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A tracer is a radioactive substance used in PET scans to highlight areas of abnormal cell activity.&lt;SEP&gt;A tracer is a radioactive sugar-based substance injected into a vein to help identify areas of cancer activity in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A tracer is a radioactive substance injected into the bloodstream to highlight areas of the body during imaging tests.&lt;SEP&gt;A tracer is a substance used in medical imaging to highlight areas of the body, such as bones.&lt;SEP&gt;A tracer is a radioactive substance injected into the body to help visualize internal structures during a PET scan.&lt;SEP&gt;A tracer is a radioactive substance injected into the vein to help visualize areas of the body during a PET scan.&lt;SEP&gt;A Tracer is a radioactive substance injected into the vein to help visualize cancer cells during a PET scan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c0bb66b1a2f93e89f5342ab1077451&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
