    </node>
    <node id="Epidermis">
      <data key="d0">Epidermis</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The epidermis is the top layer of the skin, composed of basal cells, squamous cells, and melanocytes.&lt;SEP&gt;Epidermis is the outermost layer of the skin, providing a waterproof barrier and producing melanin.&lt;SEP&gt;The epidermis is the outermost layer of the skin.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6eafb110f88c7af38808f77f59ed155d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66dd071b6c2be50e36cee1a1c1bd3b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839747</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dermis">
      <data key="d0">Dermis</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The dermis is the middle layer of the skin, containing blood vessels, nerves, and sweat glands.&lt;SEP&gt;Dermis is the middle layer of the skin containing connective tissue, hair follicles, and sweat glands.&lt;SEP&gt;The dermis is the middle layer of the skin, containing blood vessels, hair follicles, and sweat glands.</data>
