    </node>
    <node id="Karnofsky Performance Status">
      <data key="d0">Karnofsky Performance Status</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Karnofsky Performance Status is a scale used to rate a patient's general health and ability to perform daily tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Karnofsky Performance Status (KPS) is a scale used to assess a patient's ability to perform daily activities and overall health.&lt;SEP&gt;The Karnofsky Performance Status is a method used to evaluate a patient's ability to perform daily activities and overall health.&lt;SEP&gt;The Karnofsky Performance Status (KPS) is a scale used to evaluate a patient's ability to perform daily tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3fbf2f6a3c150687a59f814d94f1d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d73843c009e523101e1464a2b28bc144</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
