    <node id="Premenopause">
      <data key="d0">Premenopause</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Premenopause is a stage in a woman's reproductive life where the ovaries are the main source of estrogen and progesterone, and menstrual periods may stop temporarily.&lt;SEP&gt;Premenopause refers to the period before menopause when the ovaries are the main source of estrogen and progesterone.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839755</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Amenorrhea">
      <data key="d0">Amenorrhea</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Amenorrhea is the absence of menstrual periods, which may occur during treatment or for up to 2 years afterward.&lt;SEP&gt;Amenorrhea is the absence of menstrual periods, which may occur during endocrine therapy and may return after treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
