    <node id="Extrafascial Hysterectomy">
      <data key="d0">Extrafascial Hysterectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Extrafascial hysterectomy is a surgical procedure recommended for certain stages of cervical cancer, involving the removal of the uterus and cervix without removing surrounding tissues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839755</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="EBRT">
      <data key="d0">EBRT</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">EBRT stands for External Beam Radiation Therapy, a type of radiation treatment used in cancer therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;EBRT stands for External Beam Radiation Therapy, a form of radiation treatment that targets cancer from outside the body.&lt;SEP&gt;EBRT stands for External Beam Radiation Therapy, a type of radiation treatment that delivers high-energy X-rays to the tumor area from outside the body.&lt;SEP&gt;EBRT stands for external beam radiation therapy, a form of radiation treatment for cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;EBRT stands for External Beam Radiation Therapy, a treatment method used to target and destroy cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Modified Radical Hysterectomy">
      <data key="d0">Modified Radical Hysterectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Modified radical hysterectomy is a surgical procedure involving the removal of the uterus, cervix, and surrounding tissues, often including lymph node removal.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radical Hysterectomy">
      <data key="d0">Radical Hysterectomy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Radical hysterectomy is a more extensive surgical procedure than a simple hysterectomy, typically involving the removal of the uterus, cervix, upper part of the vagina, and nearby lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Radical hysterectomy is a surgical procedure that removes the uterus, cervix, and surrounding tissues, often used in gynecological cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d0e32bdc49dbab9c2c953abf363e317</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pelvic Lymph Node Evaluation">
      <data key="d0">Pelvic Lymph Node Evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Pelvic Lymph Node Evaluation is a procedure to check for cancer spread to pelvic lymph nodes.&lt;SEP&gt;Pelvic lymph node evaluation is a procedure to examine lymph nodes in the pelvis for signs of cancer spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Para-Aortic Nodes">
      <data key="d0">Para-Aortic Nodes</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Para-aortic nodes are lymph nodes located in the abdomen and may be removed during surgical staging for cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Para-Aortic Nodes are lymph nodes located near the aorta and may be removed during surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;Para-aortic nodes are lymph nodes located near the aorta in the abdomen, often examined for cancer metastasis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 1A1">
      <data key="d0">Stage 1A1</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 1A1 is a classification of cervical cancer that indicates cancer is confined to the cervix and is small in size.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1A1 is a sub-stage of Stage 1A cervical cancer, indicating cancer that is small and has not spread beyond the cervix.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 1A2">
      <data key="d0">Stage 1A2</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 1A2 is a classification of cervical cancer that indicates cancer is slightly larger but still confined to the cervix.&lt;SEP&gt;Stage 1A2 is a sub-stage of Stage 1A cervical cancer, indicating cancer that is slightly larger but still confined to the cervix.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LVSI">
      <data key="d0">LVSI</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">LVSI stands for Lymphovascular Space Invasion, a factor indicating the presence of cancer cells in blood or lymph vessels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Small Cell Neuroendocrine Carcinoma of the Cervix">
      <data key="d0">Small Cell Neuroendocrine Carcinoma of the Cervix</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Small cell neuroendocrine carcinoma of the cervix is a rare and aggressive type of cervical cancer that grows quickly and spreads early.&lt;SEP&gt;Small cell neuroendocrine carcinoma of the cervix (NECC) is a rare and aggressive form of cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Platinum Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d0">Platinum Chemotherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Platinum chemotherapy is a type of chemotherapy that uses platinum-based drugs to treat various cancers, including cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vaginal Brachytherapy">
      <data key="d0">Vaginal Brachytherapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Vaginal brachytherapy is a form of radiation therapy that delivers radiation directly to the vaginal area, often used in the treatment of cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Surgical Staging">
      <data key="d0">Surgical Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Surgical staging is a procedure to determine the extent of cancer spread during surgery.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgical staging is a process used to determine the extent of cancer based on tissue and lymph node analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Surgical staging is a procedure where lymph nodes are surgically removed and tested to determine the extent of cancer spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ac570b4029abb181150e0d0975aefb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Follow-Up Visits">
      <data key="d0">Follow-Up Visits</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Follow-up visits are scheduled medical appointments after treatment for cervical cancer to monitor for recurrence and assess overall health.&lt;SEP&gt;Follow-up visits are scheduled appointments for monitoring after cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Follow-up visits are regular check-ups to monitor the progress of a glioma and adjust treatment as needed.&lt;SEP&gt;Follow-up visits are scheduled medical check-ups used to monitor a patient's condition after treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3ba7430f3a31330247f52afe7e9c68a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Physical Exams">
      <data key="d0">Physical Exams</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Physical exams are medical evaluations performed by healthcare professionals to assess a patient's health status.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839756</data>
