    </node>
    <node id="Cerebrospinal Fluid">
      <data key="d0">Cerebrospinal Fluid</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Cerebrospinal fluid is a liquid that surrounds and protects the brain and spinal cord.&lt;SEP&gt;Cerebrospinal fluid is a clear liquid that surrounds the brain and spinal cord.&lt;SEP&gt;Cerebrospinal fluid is a liquid that surrounds the brain and spinal cord, often tested for cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Cerebrospinal fluid is a protective liquid that surrounds the brain and spinal cord, analyzed during a lumbar puncture to detect cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Cerebrospinal fluid is a clear liquid surrounding the brain and spinal cord, where cancer cells may be found and treated with intrathecal chemotherapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fba176235a4410ba8723447134c92579</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839763</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Eyes">
      <data key="d0">Eyes</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Eyes are the organs responsible for vision, and are examined during a physical exam.&lt;SEP&gt;Eyes are organs responsible for vision.&lt;SEP&gt;The eyes can be affected by primary CNS lymphoma, leading to vision changes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839763</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Neurological Symptoms">
      <data key="d0">Neurological Symptoms</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Neurological symptoms are signs of issues affecting the nervous system, such as headaches, seizures, or coordination problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Neurological symptoms include issues with coordination, movement, personality changes, memory problems, and difficulty speaking or swallowing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839763</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Headaches">
      <data key="d0">Headaches</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Headaches are a common neurological symptom associated with primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Headaches are a common symptom of brain tumors, often caused by increased pressure within the skull.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839763</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Seizures">
      <data key="d0">Seizures</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Seizures are neurological events that can result from pressure caused by a lymphoma tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;Seizures are sudden, uncontrolled electrical disturbances in the brain that can cause changes in behavior, movement, or consciousness.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839763</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Blurred Vision">
      <data key="d0">Blurred Vision</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Blurred vision is a condition where visual clarity is reduced, making it difficult to see details clearly.&lt;SEP&gt;Blurred vision is a visual symptom that may occur due to primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Blurred vision is a vision problem that can be caused by gliomas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839763</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Double Vision">
      <data key="d0">Double Vision</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Double vision is a visual symptom that may occur due to primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Double vision is a vision problem that may be associated with gliomas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
