    <node id="Central Nervous System">
      <data key="d0">Central Nervous System</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Central Nervous System includes the brain and spinal cord, and is considered the control center for the body's functions. It is a critical part of the nervous system responsible for processing information and coordinating bodily activities. Some descriptions also mention that the Central Nervous System includes cerebrospinal fluid, though this is not universally stated. The Central Nervous System can be affected by various diseases, including acute lymphoblastic leukemia, gliomas, and primary CNS lymphoma. Primary CNS lymphoma originates in the Central Nervous System, as does certain types of tumors. These conditions highlight the system's importance in both normal physiological function and in the development of specific pathologies. The Central Nervous System consists of the brain and spinal cord, with multiple descriptions confirming this core structure. While there are variations in the details provided, the consensus remains that the brain and spinal cord form the central components of this system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4966a628b12ecec4187796598764cf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d4d6b091e033fd01aa721422b68ef5</data>
