    <node id="Digital Rectal Exam">
      <data key="d0">Digital Rectal Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Digital Rectal Exam is a medical procedure used to examine the rectum and anus for abnormalities. It involves a doctor inserting a gloved finger into the rectum to check the prostate for any signs of issues. The exam is primarily conducted to assess the size and texture of the prostate, which can help in detecting conditions such as cancer. In some descriptions, the procedure is referred to as a physical examination where a doctor checks the prostate for abnormalities. The process typically includes the insertion of a gloved finger into the rectum, and it may also involve examining the rectum itself for irregularities. The Digital Rectal Exam (DRE) is widely recognized as an important diagnostic tool in men's health, particularly for early detection of prostate-related diseases. While most descriptions focus on the prostate, some mention the broader examination of the rectum and anus. Overall, the procedure is performed by healthcare professionals and is considered a standard part of a physical exam for certain medical evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aeafa486bfd320cdaa7811ad75777912&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839767</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
