    <node id="Pelvic MRI">
      <data key="d0">Pelvic MRI</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Pelvic MRI is a diagnostic imaging technique used to assess rectal cancer and guide treatment decisions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839767</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Flexible Sigmoidoscopy">
      <data key="d0">Flexible Sigmoidoscopy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Flexible sigmoidoscopy is a procedure used to examine the lower part of the colon for signs of cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839767</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Information">
      <data key="d0">Medical Information</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Medical information refers to verified, professionally reviewed health-related content provided by reputable sources.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839767</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Endoscopic Ultrasound">
      <data key="d0">Endoscopic Ultrasound</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Endoscopic ultrasound is a diagnostic technique used to evaluate the depth of rectal cancer and surrounding tissues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839767</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Transabdominal Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Transabdominal Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Transabdominal surgery is a surgical procedure used to treat rectal cancer when local excision is not sufficient.&lt;SEP&gt;Transabdominal surgery is a treatment option for tumors that have invaded the muscle layer of the rectal wall.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f2c9770fd98dbbe3c7947601fb3e654c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839767</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NPC">
      <data key="d0">NPC</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">NPC is a type of cancer that affects the nasopharynx, a region connecting the nasal cavity to the pharynx.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839767</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nasopharynx">
      <data key="d0">Nasopharynx</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The nasopharynx is the upper part of the pharynx, located behind the nose and nasal cavity.&lt;SEP&gt;The nasopharynx is the area at the back of the nose that connects to the back of the mouth.&lt;SEP&gt;The nasopharynx is the area connecting the nasal cavity to the back of the mouth, where nasopharyngeal carcinoma originates.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9383db20cd696688798a193862cb5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fertility Testing">
      <data key="d0">Fertility Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Fertility testing is a set of medical procedures to assess reproductive health and potential.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertility testing is conducted for all genders to assess reproductive health before cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anal Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Anal Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Anal Cancer is a type of cancer that develops in the tissues of the anus, anal canal, or perianal region. It is often linked to human papillomavirus (HPV) infection, with certain strains of the virus being identified as a contributing factor. This rare form of cancer can originate in the anal canal or surrounding areas and may spread to lymph nodes or other parts of the body. Anal Cancer is typically treated with chemoradiation or surgery, depending on the stage and severity of the condition. The term "anal cancer" also encompasses cancers affecting the broader anal region, which are addressed in survivorship resources. Descriptions consistently highlight its association with HPV, its potential for metastasis, and its treatment approaches. While some descriptions emphasize its rarity, others focus on its origin and progression. Overall, Anal Cancer is a malignancy that arises in the anal tissues and requires targeted medical intervention.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44a870810cef881997b741c32ec368fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf41d1c08e8df109ad214d831867a5d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d4cea71149e0e4157126efdaa0ea3e3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Epstein-Barr Virus (EBV) DNA Testing">
      <data key="d0">Epstein-Barr Virus (EBV) DNA Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">EBV DNA testing is used to detect the presence of the Epstein-Barr virus, which is associated with NPC.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nutrition, Speech, and Swallowing Evaluation">
      <data key="d0">Nutrition, Speech, and Swallowing Evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">These evaluations assess how cancer and its treatment may affect a patient's ability to eat, speak, and swallow.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Eye and Endocrine Evaluation">
      <data key="d0">Eye and Endocrine Evaluation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">An eye and endocrine evaluation checks for any complications related to vision and hormonal function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tobacco and Alcohol Use History">
      <data key="d0">Tobacco and Alcohol Use History</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tobacco and alcohol use history is a critical factor in assessing cancer risk and treatment outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Tobacco and alcohol use history is a record of a patient's past and current use of these substances, which are risk factors for head and neck cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Tobacco and alcohol use are risk factors for head and neck cancers and are assessed during the medical evaluation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Comprehensive Cancer Center">
      <data key="d0">Comprehensive Cancer Center</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">A comprehensive cancer center is a specialized facility with experts in evaluating and treating nasopharyngeal carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Insurance Provider">
      <data key="d0">Insurance Provider</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">An insurance provider is a company that offers coverage for medical treatments and services.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Head and Neck Exam">
      <data key="d0">Head and Neck Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A head and neck exam is a physical assessment of the head, neck, and related structures to detect signs of disease.&lt;SEP&gt;A head and neck exam is part of the physical examination to assess for signs of cancer in the head and neck area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mirror Exam">
      <data key="d0">Mirror Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A mirror exam is used during a head and neck examination to visualize areas of the throat that are not easily seen.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Screen for Depression">
      <data key="d0">Screen for Depression</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Screening for depression is part of the assessment process to evaluate a patient's mental health.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nasopharyngeal Fiberoptic Exam">
      <data key="d0">Nasopharyngeal Fiberoptic Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A nasopharyngeal fiberoptic exam uses a flexible scope to examine the nasopharynx for abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MRI with Contrast">
      <data key="d0">MRI with Contrast</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">MRI with contrast is a diagnostic tool used to assess the extent of cancer in the head and neck region.&lt;SEP&gt;An MRI with contrast is used to evaluate the tumor and surrounding tissues in detail.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CT of Skull Base and Neck">
      <data key="d0">CT of Skull Base and Neck</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A CT scan of the skull base and neck is performed to assess the extent of the tumor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chest CT with Contrast">
      <data key="d0">Chest CT with Contrast</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A chest CT with contrast is used to check for cancer spread to the lungs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839768</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dental Work">
      <data key="d0">Dental Work</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Dental work refers to procedures performed on the teeth and gums, which may be affected by head and neck cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Smoking Cessation Help">
      <data key="d0">Smoking Cessation Help</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Smoking cessation help provides support and resources to quit tobacco use, which is critical for cancer treatment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fertility Counseling">
      <data key="d0">Fertility Counseling</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Fertility counseling is provided to patients to discuss reproductive health during cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertility counseling is a service that helps patients understand and manage fertility concerns related to cancer treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Fertility counseling offers guidance on preserving reproductive health before cancer treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47a420aa2acde1175ad95bf6dc2e664</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tobacco Use">
      <data key="d0">Tobacco Use</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tobacco use is a significant risk factor for developing head and neck cancers and can affect treatment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Alcohol Use">
      <data key="d0">Alcohol Use</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Alcohol use is another risk factor for head and neck cancers and is monitored during medical evaluations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Special Mirror">
      <data key="d0">Special Mirror</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A special mirror is used during exams to help visualize hard-to-see areas of the throat.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fiberoptic Scope">
      <data key="d0">Fiberoptic Scope</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A Fiberoptic Scope is a medical instrument used to visualize internal body areas, such as the oral cavity and throat.&lt;SEP&gt;A fiberoptic scope is a flexible instrument used to examine internal body structures, such as the nasopharynx.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711bee9440e11d7c737bc4a49b880910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Breast Milk">
      <data key="d0">Breast Milk</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Breast milk is a fluid produced by the mammary glands of the breast for nourishing infants.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nipple">
      <data key="d0">Nipple</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The nipple is the raised tip of the areola and serves as the opening for milk ducts.&lt;SEP&gt;The nipple is the central part of the breast through which breast milk is expelled.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dc8d8e5ed4f165f3e56305a7644ba05</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Clinical Breast Exam">
      <data key="d0">Clinical Breast Exam</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A clinical breast exam is a physical examination of the breasts performed by a healthcare provider to detect abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5846f51c2ca4fae54459ce9c50e3e820</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Autoimmune Disease">
      <data key="d0">Autoimmune Disease</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An autoimmune disease is a condition where the immune system attacks healthy tissues and organs.&lt;SEP&gt;An autoimmune disease is a condition where the immune system attacks the body's own cells, potentially increasing cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Meninges">
      <data key="d0">Meninges</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Meninges are protective membranes that cover the brain and spinal cord.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skull">
      <data key="d0">Skull</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The skull is a bony structure that protects the brain and is mentioned as a potential site for cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;The skull is a bony structure that protects the brain.&lt;SEP&gt;The skull is the bony structure that protects the brain and is involved in craniotomy procedures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9882c04dd7676c6433074e5e393c72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffc3446f8ec092af24a460bda94f772f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vertebrae">
      <data key="d0">Vertebrae</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Vertebrae are the bones that make up the spine and protect the spinal cord.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839769</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Genetic Abnormality">
      <data key="d0">Genetic Abnormality</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A genetic abnormality is a mutation in DNA that can lead to uncontrolled cell growth and cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Immunodeficiency Disorder">
      <data key="d0">Immunodeficiency Disorder</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An immunodeficiency disorder is a condition that weakens the immune system's ability to fight infections.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bladder Control">
      <data key="d0">Bladder Control</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bladder control refers to the ability to manage urination and prevent incontinence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Speech Difficulty">
      <data key="d0">Speech Difficulty</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Speech difficulty refers to challenges in speaking clearly or communicating effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Speech difficulty is a symptom of gliomas, often linked to the location of the tumor in the brain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Swallowing Difficulty">
      <data key="d0">Swallowing Difficulty</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Swallowing difficulty refers to trouble consuming food or liquids without choking or discomfort.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Eye Sight">
      <data key="d0">Eye Sight</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Eye sight refers to the ability to see clearly and perceive visual information.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Headache">
      <data key="d0">Headache</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A headache is a pain or discomfort in the head, often caused by pressure or tension in the nerves or muscles.&lt;SEP&gt;Headache is a common symptom of gliomas, often occurring in the morning or waking the patient at night.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Seizure">
      <data key="d0">Seizure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A seizure is a sudden, uncontrolled electrical disturbance in the brain that can cause changes in behavior, movement, or consciousness.&lt;SEP&gt;Seizure is a frequent symptom of gliomas, especially in low-grade cases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PSA Testing">
      <data key="d0">PSA Testing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">PSA Testing is a medical procedure that measures the level of prostate-specific antigen in the blood to detect potential prostate issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839770</data>
