    </node>
    <node id="Prostate-Specific Antigen">
      <data key="d0">Prostate-Specific Antigen</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Prostate-specific antigen (PSA) is a protein produced by the prostate gland, measured in blood tests to detect potential prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate-Specific Antigen (PSA) is a protein produced by the prostate gland, and elevated levels may indicate prostate cancer or other conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate-specific antigen (PSA) is a protein produced by the prostate gland, and elevated levels may indicate prostate cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Prostate-specific antigen (PSA) is a protein produced by the prostate gland, used as a marker in diagnosing and monitoring prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9dc281a303d0d4c5300c0c1c45b739ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697db1653f51e966e79b92eefeb01ec6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6232dd9ed168a1113955e7300645338b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7</data>
