    <node id="Prostate Cancer Basics">
      <data key="d0">Prostate Cancer Basics</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Prostate Cancer Basics is an overview of what prostate cancer is, its causes, symptoms, and treatment options.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839771</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thyroid Nodule">
      <data key="d0">Thyroid Nodule</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">A thyroid nodule is an abnormal growth in the thyroid gland that can be benign or malignant.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839771</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thyroid Hormone">
      <data key="d0">Thyroid Hormone</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Thyroid hormone is a hormone produced by the thyroid gland that regulates metabolism and other bodily functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839771</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TSH">
      <data key="d0">TSH</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">TSH (Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone) is a hormone produced by the pituitary gland that stimulates the thyroid to produce thyroid hormones.&lt;SEP&gt;TSH stands for Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone, a hormone that regulates the production of thyroid hormones.&lt;SEP&gt;TSH is a hormone that regulates thyroid function and is kept at low levels through medication.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839771</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hyperthyroidism">
      <data key="d0">Hyperthyroidism</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Hyperthyroidism is a condition where the thyroid produces excessive amounts of hormones, often indicated by low TSH levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Hyperthyroidism is a condition where the thyroid gland produces excessive amounts of thyroid hormone, leading to symptoms such as weight loss, rapid heartbeat, and anxiety.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radioactive Iodine Uptake Test">
      <data key="d0">Radioactive Iodine Uptake Test</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The radioactive iodine uptake test is used to evaluate thyroid function and detect potential abnormalities.&lt;SEP&gt;The radioactive iodine uptake test measures how much iodine the thyroid absorbs, helping diagnose thyroid function and detect abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Papillary Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Papillary Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Papillary carcinoma is the most common type of thyroid cancer, characterized by slow-growing tumors with a favorable prognosis.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Follicular Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Follicular Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Follicular carcinoma is a type of thyroid cancer that arises from the follicular cells of the thyroid and tends to grow more slowly than some other types.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medullary Thyroid Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Medullary Thyroid Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Medullary thyroid cancer is a rare type of thyroid cancer that originates from the parafollicular C cells and can be inherited.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anaplastic Thyroid Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Anaplastic Thyroid Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Anaplastic thyroid cancer is a highly aggressive and rare form of thyroid cancer that typically affects older adults.&lt;SEP&gt;Anaplastic thyroid cancer is a rare and aggressive form of thyroid cancer that is often treated with radiation therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Anaplastic thyroid cancer is a rare and aggressive form of thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Neck Dissection">
      <data key="d0">Neck Dissection</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A neck dissection is a surgical procedure that removes lymph nodes in the neck if they are suspected to contain cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Suppression">
      <data key="d0">Suppression</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Suppression refers to the practice of keeping TSH levels low to prevent the growth or recurrence of thyroid cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Suppression is a medical strategy used in thyroid cancer treatment to lower TSH levels and prevent cancer recurrence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Radioactive Iodine">
      <data key="d0">Radioactive Iodine</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Radioactive iodine is a substance used in the treatment of certain types of thyroid cancer to destroy remaining thyroid tissue or cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Radioactive iodine (iodine-131) is a treatment used to destroy thyroid cancer cells that absorb iodine.&lt;SEP&gt;Radioactive Iodine (RAI) is a treatment used for certain types of thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e017cd4fd8af1ebbcb582a93fbfe1ea</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Isthmus">
      <data key="d0">Isthmus</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The isthmus is the tissue connecting the two lobes of the thyroid gland.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hypoparathyroidism">
      <data key="d0">Hypoparathyroidism</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Hypoparathyroidism is a condition characterized by low levels of calcium in the blood, often resulting from damage to the parathyroid glands during thyroid surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Voice and Swallowing Nerves">
      <data key="d0">Voice and Swallowing Nerves</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The nerves controlling voice and swallowing can be damaged during thyroid surgery, leading to potential complications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="HPV">
      <data key="d0">HPV</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Human papillomavirus (HPV) is a virus associated with certain types of cancer, including throat cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;HPV is a virus associated with certain types of cancer, including throat cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;HPV stands for Human Papillomavirus, a sexually transmitted infection strongly associated with cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;HPV is a sexually transmitted virus that can lead to various cancers, including anal cancer, if it causes long-term cell changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Human papillomavirus (HPV) is a group of viruses that can cause various cancers, including anal cancer, and has over 100 strains.&lt;SEP&gt;HPV is a sexually transmitted virus strongly linked to the development of anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a44e885faf856aa579d824b3cd85e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Immunosuppressant Use">
      <data key="d0">Immunosuppressant Use</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Use of immunosuppressants increases the risk of anal cancer by weakening the immune system.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunosuppressant use is a risk factor for anal cancer due to weakened immune function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="DRE">
      <data key="d0">DRE</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">DRE is a physical examination method used to detect abnormalities in the anal region.&lt;SEP&gt;DRE (Digital Rectal Exam) is a physical examination where a doctor inserts a gloved finger into the rectum to check for abnormalities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anoscopy">
      <data key="d0">Anoscopy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Anoscopy is a procedure used to examine the anal canal and surrounding areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Anoscopy is a medical procedure used to examine the anal canal and is recommended for follow-up after treatment for anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Anoscopy is a procedure used to examine the anus and detect anal cancer recurrence.&lt;SEP&gt;Anoscopy is a medical procedure that involves examining the anus and lower rectum with a specialized instrument.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839773</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Linear Accelerator">
      <data key="d0">Linear Accelerator</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A linear accelerator is a machine used in radiation therapy to generate high-energy radiation beams.&lt;SEP&gt;A linear accelerator is a machine used in external beam radiation therapy to deliver high-energy radiation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839773</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bowel Function">
      <data key="d0">Bowel Function</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bowel function can be affected as a long-term side effect of radiation therapy for anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839773</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bladder Function">
      <data key="d0">Bladder Function</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bladder function may be affected as a long-term side effect of radiation therapy for anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839773</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Simulation">
      <data key="d0">Simulation</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Simulation is a planning session before external beam radiation therapy to determine the treatment plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Simulation is a planning session before radiation therapy that involves imaging to map the treatment area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b0bad5ee25cb854c10bdbc9d33b54a1a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839773</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Frog-Legged Position">
