    <node id="Local Excision">
      <data key="d0">Local Excision</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Local excision is a surgical procedure to remove a tumor, sometimes requiring additional treatment based on tissue analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Local excision is a surgical procedure that removes only the tumor and surrounding tissue for certain early-stage perianal cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;Local excision is a surgical procedure used for low-grade (G1) and intermediate-grade (G2) perianal cancers when the surgical margin is clear of cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Local excision is a surgical procedure to remove small tumors or abnormal tissue without removing the entire affected area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6236b93e627d54f73f1c8fe341127e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fdcce851d69aa713ed64ba1895bd5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
