    </node>
    <node id="Low Anterior Resection">
      <data key="d0">Low Anterior Resection</data>
      <data key="d1">procedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Low anterior resection is a type of transabdominal surgery used to remove tumors in the mid to upper rectum.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839774</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rectal Tumor">
      <data key="d0">Rectal Tumor</data>
      <data key="d1">condition</data>
      <data key="d2">A rectal tumor is a growth in the rectum that may require surgical removal and further treatment based on its stage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839774</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T2 Tumor">
      <data key="d0">T2 Tumor</data>
      <data key="d1">condition</data>
      <data key="d2">A T2 tumor is a rectal tumor that has invaded the muscle layer of the rectal wall.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839774</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T1 Tumor">
      <data key="d0">T1 Tumor</data>
      <data key="d1">condition</data>
      <data key="d2">A T1 tumor is a smaller rectal tumor that may be treated with abdominal surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839774</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="T3 Cancer">
      <data key="d0">T3 Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">condition</data>
      <data key="d2">T3 cancer refers to larger rectal tumors that have not spread to lymph nodes but may require surgery.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839774</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Oxaliplatin">
      <data key="d0">Oxaliplatin</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Oxaliplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in the treatment of ovarian cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxaliplatin is a chemotherapy drug that can cause nerve damage in the fingers and toes.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxaliplatin is a chemotherapy drug used in the FOLFOX regimen for metastatic anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxaliplatin is a platinum-based chemotherapy drug used in the treatment of various cancers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b69d38fafe014cece3427bd0459ae42b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839774</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Irinotecan">
      <data key="d0">Irinotecan</data>
      <data key="d1">drug</data>
      <data key="d2">Irinotecan is a chemotherapy drug known to cause side effects such as abdominal cramping, nausea, diarrhea, and hair loss.&lt;SEP&gt;Irinotecan is a chemotherapy drug that can cause gastrointestinal side effects and hair loss.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839774</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Kidney Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Kidney Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">condition</data>
      <data key="d2">Kidney cancer is a type of cancer that originates in the tissues of the kidneys, with renal cell carcinoma being the most common form.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney cancer is a type of cancer that affects the kidneys, with various subtypes and stages.&lt;SEP&gt;Kidney cancer is a group of cancers that originate in the kidneys, with various subtypes and behaviors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839774</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RCC Subtypes">
      <data key="d0">RCC Subtypes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">RCC subtypes refer to different types of renal cell carcinoma, a form of kidney cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839774</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pathologic Staging">
      <data key="d0">Pathologic Staging</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Pathologic staging is the classification of cancer based on laboratory analysis of removed tissues.&lt;SEP&gt;Pathologic staging is performed after surgery and involves examining tissue removed during the procedure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-37bca9f4d2ebaeed359c9b4eb7a0c1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839774</data>
      <data key="d6" />
