    <node id="Stereotactic Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Stereotactic Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A stereotactic biopsy is a precise procedure used to obtain tissue samples from hard-to-reach brain tumors.&lt;SEP&gt;Stereotactic biopsy is a procedure used to diagnose primary CNS lymphoma by removing a tumor sample.&lt;SEP&gt;A stereotactic biopsy is a precise technique used to obtain tissue samples from hard-to-reach areas of the brain.&lt;SEP&gt;A stereotactic biopsy is a procedure used to remove a small sample of a tumor for diagnostic purposes, guided by imaging technology.&lt;SEP&gt;A stereotactic biopsy is a precise procedure used to obtain a tumor sample.</data>
