      <data key="d2">Myeloid blasts are immature white blood cells that are abnormal in AML.&lt;SEP&gt;Myeloid blasts are immature white blood cells that can accumulate in the bone marrow and blood in cases of leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Myeloid blasts are immature white blood cells that are typically found in the bone marrow.&lt;SEP&gt;Myeloid blasts are immature white blood cells that may indicate the presence of AML.</data>
