    <node id="Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia">
      <data key="d0">Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chronic lymphocytic leukemia is a type of cancer affecting white blood cells in the bone marrow, which can weaken the immune system.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) is a type of blood cancer that grows slowly and affects B cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) is a type of cancer that affects blood and bone marrow, often requiring monitoring or treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia is a type of cancer that affects B cells in the blood and bone marrow.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin Shave Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Skin Shave Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A skin shave biopsy removes the top layer of skin and part of the dermis using a razor-like tool, used for flat skin lesions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tobacco Smoke">
      <data key="d0">Tobacco Smoke</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Tobacco smoke is an environmental toxin that can contribute to the development of squamous cell skin cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Tobacco smoke is an environmental toxin that can cause skin damage and increase the risk of squamous cell carcinoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Tobacco Smoke is a substance containing over 50 cancer-causing compounds, primarily linked to lung cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Car Exhaust">
      <data key="d0">Car Exhaust</data>
      <data key="d1">environmentalfactor</data>
      <data key="d2">Car exhaust is an environmental pollutant that can contribute to skin damage and increase the risk of skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Arsenic">
      <data key="d0">Arsenic</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Arsenic is a toxic element found in soil, water, and air that increases the risk of squamous cell carcinoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Arsenic is a toxic element found in soil, water, and air, and can cause skin damage leading to squamous cell carcinoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Arsenic is a toxic metal that can increase the risk of lung cancer when exposed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7843955573cdc294b34e74019195fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ulcers">
      <data key="d0">Ulcers</data>
      <data key="d1">medicalcondition</data>
      <data key="d2">Ulcers are chronic wounds that can become sites for squamous cell skin cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Ulcers are chronic wounds that can develop into Marjolin’s ulcer, a type of squamous cell carcinoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Organ Transplantation">
      <data key="d0">Organ Transplantation</data>
      <data key="d1">medicalprocedure</data>
      <data key="d2">Organ transplantation is a medical procedure that often requires immunosuppressant drugs, which can increase the risk of skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Immunosuppressants">
      <data key="d0">Immunosuppressants</data>
      <data key="d1">medicaltreatment</data>
      <data key="d2">Immunosuppressants are drugs used after organ transplantation that reduce the body's ability to fight infections and diseases, increasing the risk of skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Local Anesthetic">
      <data key="d0">Local Anesthetic</data>
      <data key="d1">medicaltreatment</data>
      <data key="d2">A local anesthetic is a medication used to numb the area during a skin biopsy, reducing discomfort.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3821a6febf2d21784059ac62a6e659c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="IRI">
      <data key="d0">IRI</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">IRI is a term used in medical regimens to indicate the presence of irinotecan, a chemotherapy drug.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Clear Cell RCC">
      <data key="d0">Clear Cell RCC</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Clear cell RCC (ccRCC) is the most common subtype of renal cell carcinoma, characterized by pale or clear cells under a microscope.&lt;SEP&gt;Clear Cell RCC (ccRCC) is the most common subtype of renal cell carcinoma, characterized by pale or clear cells under a microscope.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Clear Cell RCC">
      <data key="d0">Non-Clear Cell RCC</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-clear cell RCC (nccRCC) refers to subtypes of renal cell carcinoma that are not clear cell, with several distinct categories.&lt;SEP&gt;Non-Clear Cell RCC (nccRCC) includes various subtypes such as Papillary RCC, Chromophobe RCC, and others, differing from Clear Cell RCC in cellular appearance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Renal Capsule">
      <data key="d0">Renal Capsule</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The renal capsule is a thin layer of tissue covering the kidney, similar to the skin of an apple.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urinary System">
      <data key="d0">Urinary System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The urinary system is a group of organs including the kidneys, ureters, bladder, and urethra that work together to remove waste from the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Renal Artery">
      <data key="d0">Renal Artery</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The renal artery is a blood vessel that carries blood with waste into the kidney.&lt;SEP&gt;The renal artery is a blood vessel that carries blood to the kidneys.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Renal Tubules">
      <data key="d0">Renal Tubules</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Renal tubules are tiny filtering tubes within the kidney where blood is cleaned and waste is removed.&lt;SEP&gt;Renal tubules are small tubes in the kidneys responsible for filtering waste from the blood and producing urine.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839779</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Renal Pelvis">
      <data key="d0">Renal Pelvis</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The renal pelvis is a hollow space in the middle of the kidney where urine collects before leaving the kidney.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ureter">
      <data key="d0">Ureter</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The ureter is a long tube that carries urine from the kidney to the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adrenal Gland">
      <data key="d0">Adrenal Gland</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The adrenal gland is a small organ located on top of each kidney, surrounded by fat and fibrous tissue.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gerotas Fascia">
      <data key="d0">Gerotas Fascia</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Gerota’s fascia is an outer layer of fibrous tissue that surrounds the kidney and adrenal glands.&lt;SEP&gt;Gerota’s fascia is a layer of connective tissue surrounding the kidneys.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vena Cava">
      <data key="d0">Vena Cava</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The vena cava is a large vein that carries clean blood back to the heart after it has been filtered by the kidneys.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wilms Tumor">
      <data key="d0">Wilms Tumor</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Wilms tumor (nephroblastoma) is a type of kidney cancer that typically occurs in young children.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Renal Sarcoma">
      <data key="d0">Renal Sarcoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Renal sarcoma is a rare type of cancer that originates in the blood vessels or connective tissue of the kidney.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Urothelial Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Urothelial Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Urothelial carcinoma is a type of cancer that starts in the cells lining the renal pelvis and ureter, often associated with bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Renal Vein">
      <data key="d0">Renal Vein</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The renal vein is a blood vessel that carries clean, filtered blood out of the kidney.&lt;SEP&gt;The renal vein is a blood vessel that carries filtered blood away from the kidneys.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Transitional Cell Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Transitional Cell Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Transitional cell cancer is an older term for urothelial carcinoma, which shares features with bladder cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inch">
      <data key="d0">Inch</data>
      <data key="d1">unit</data>
      <data key="d2">An inch is a unit of length equal to half a centimeter.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 0 Anal Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Stage 0 Anal Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 0 anal cancer is a precancerous condition where abnormal cells are present on the surface of the anal canal or perianal region.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839780</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Anal Dysplasia">
      <data key="d0">Anal Dysplasia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Anal dysplasia refers to abnormal cell growth in or near the anus, which can be pre-cancerous and may lead to anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Anal dysplasia is a precancerous condition involving abnormal cell growth in the anal area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839781</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="High-Grade Anal Intraepithelial Neoplasia">
      <data key="d0">High-Grade Anal Intraepithelial Neoplasia</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">High-grade anal intraepithelial neoplasia is a precancerous condition characterized by abnormal cell growth in the anal canal.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839781</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="High-Grade Squamous Intraepithelial Lesions">
      <data key="d0">High-Grade Squamous Intraepithelial Lesions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">High-grade squamous intraepithelial lesions are precancerous changes in the cells lining the anal canal.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839781</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Electrocautery">
      <data key="d0">Electrocautery</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Electrocautery is a treatment method used to remove abnormal tissue using heat.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839781</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Surgical Removal">
      <data key="d0">Surgical Removal</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Surgical removal is a treatment option for precancerous or cancerous lesions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839781</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage I Anal Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Stage I Anal Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage I anal cancer is characterized by a tumor 2 cm or smaller that has not spread to nearby lymph nodes or distant areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839781</data>
