    <node id="World Health Organization Classification">
      <data key="d0">World Health Organization Classification</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The World Health Organization (WHO) classifies follicular lymphoma into grades 1, 2, and 3A as classic FL (cFL).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="International Consensus Classification">
      <data key="d0">International Consensus Classification</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The International Consensus Classification (ICC) groups grades 1 and 2 of follicular lymphoma as classic FL (cFL).&lt;SEP&gt;International Consensus Classification is a system used to categorize follicular lymphoma grades.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inflammation">
      <data key="d0">Inflammation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Inflammation is a biological response to harmful stimuli, such as infection or injury, and is part of the immune system's defense mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Inflammation is a biological response to injury or infection, which can appear as bright spots on PET scans.&lt;SEP&gt;Inflammation is a physical reaction of the body to harmful stimuli, such as infection or injury.&lt;SEP&gt;Inflammation is a possible side effect of intraocular chemotherapy, often managed with medication.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2778e34af702d49d5e70867726e14b2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Diffuse Large B-Cell Lymphoma">
      <data key="d0">Diffuse Large B-Cell Lymphoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Diffuse Large B-Cell Lymphoma (DLBCL) is a fast-growing cancer that can develop from NLPHL.&lt;SEP&gt;Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) is a type of lymphoma that can be distinguished from follicular lymphoma based on cell characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) is an aggressive form of cancer that can develop from CLL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67bee20d5e5400994f8c8f03052dd06</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Extranodal Disease">
      <data key="d0">Extranodal Disease</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Extranodal disease refers to cancer that forms outside of the lymph nodes, such as in the bone marrow.&lt;SEP&gt;Extranodal disease refers to cancer that has spread beyond the lymph nodes into other tissues or organs.&lt;SEP&gt;Extranodal disease refers to the spread of disease outside the lymph nodes, often observed in older persons with lymphomas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ba71a5181f3814dffb21d3399441bea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Classic FL">
      <data key="d0">Classic FL</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Classic FL is a classification of follicular lymphoma that includes grades 1, 2, and 3A according to the WHO5 classification.&lt;SEP&gt;Classic FL refers to follicular lymphoma classified under specific grading systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Transformed FL">
      <data key="d0">Transformed FL</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Transformed FL is a more aggressive form of follicular lymphoma that may require different treatment approaches.&lt;SEP&gt;Transformed FL is a form of follicular lymphoma that progresses into a more aggressive type of lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-829d6b7840e9f2c8d97d22d2ce2c43c1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Individualized">
      <data key="d0">Individualized</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Individualized refers to a treatment approach tailored to the specific characteristics of a patient's follicular lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b00f93aa3d24d0275d4290db3fb2cca3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LHRH Agonist Anti-Androgen">
      <data key="d0">LHRH Agonist Anti-Androgen</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">LHRH Agonist Anti-Androgen combines the effects of an LHRH agonist and an anti-androgen to block testosterone.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="LHRH Antagonist">
      <data key="d0">LHRH Antagonist</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">LHRH Antagonist directly blocks the action of luteinizing hormone-releasing hormone, reducing testosterone production.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Surgical Castration">
      <data key="d0">Surgical Castration</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Surgical castration is a procedure that removes the testes, effectively blocking testosterone production.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Leuprolide (Lupron)">
      <data key="d0">Leuprolide (Lupron)</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Leuprolide (Lupron) is a commonly used LHRH agonist in the treatment of prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839784</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Degarelix (Firmagon)">
      <data key="d0">Degarelix (Firmagon)</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Degarelix (Firmagon) is a commonly used LHRH antagonist in hormone therapy for prostate cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839785</data>
