    <node id="Distant Metastasis">
      <data key="d0">Distant Metastasis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Distant metastasis refers to the spread of cancer to organs or tissues far from the original site.&lt;SEP&gt;Distant metastasis occurs when cancer spreads to distant parts of the body, such as the lungs, bones, or liver.&lt;SEP&gt;Distant metastasis occurs when cancer spreads to parts of the body far from the original tumor.&lt;SEP&gt;Distant metastasis refers to cancer spreading to body parts far from the primary tumor, such as the bone, lungs, liver, or brain.&lt;SEP&gt;Distant metastasis refers to the spread of cancer to organs such as the lungs, liver, or bones, denoted as M0 or M1.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53c0ac935ec10ce8a0839db4ad053ad1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c37f547042fc10baabdbfaadf010bce5</data>
