    <node id="Endoscopy">
      <data key="d0">Endoscopy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Endoscopy is a procedure used to examine the inside of the esophagus and collect tissue samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Endoscopy is a procedure involving examination under anesthesia to assess internal structures for cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Endoscopy is a procedure using a flexible tube with a camera to examine internal body structures, often performed under anesthesia.&lt;SEP&gt;Endoscopy involves inserting an endoscope into the body to examine internal organs, determine tumor size, and collect tissue samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Endoscopy is a medical procedure used to examine the inside of the stomach and detect abnormalities.</data>
