    <node id="Gene">
      <data key="d0">Gene</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A gene is a segment of DNA that contains instructions for making proteins, which are essential for cellular function.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene is a segment of DNA that contains instructions for making specific proteins.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene is a segment of DNA that contains instructions for making proteins, which are essential for bodily functions.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene is a segment of DNA that contains instructions for making proteins, which perform essential functions in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;A gene is a segment of DNA that contains instructions for making proteins and is responsible for inherited traits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3d609bd1a55d409470c55ad55e2d125d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0739b33959299ea67072f390ce38bffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b63f0a9aec8d42c8426ded05a9bf92b4</data>
