      <data key="d0">Capecitabine</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Capecitabine is a chemotherapy drug used in the treatment of certain cancers.&lt;SEP&gt;Capecitabine is a chemotherapy drug used in the treatment of colon cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Capecitabine is an oral chemotherapy drug taken twice daily for 5 and a half to 6 weeks during radiation therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Capecitabine is a chemotherapy drug used in combination with mitomycin for treating perianal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Capecitabine is a chemotherapy drug used in regimens for treating anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Capecitabine is a chemotherapy drug used in the treatment of anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Capecitabine is a chemotherapy drug used in the treatment of cancer, particularly as an alternative to 5-FU.</data>
