      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Mouth sores are a common side effect of systemic therapy, causing painful ulcers or sores in the mouth.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouth sores are a side effect of chemotherapy that can occur due to damage to healthy cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouth Sores are a side effect of chemotherapy due to damage to fast-growing cells in the mouth.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouth sores are a potential side effect of cisplatin treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouth sores are a common side effect of systemic therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouth sores are a common side effect of chemotherapy regimens used in the treatment of anal cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouth sores are a common side effect of chemotherapy, affecting the oral cavity and lining of the anus.</data>
