    <node id="Hair Loss">
      <data key="d0">Hair Loss</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Hair Loss is a common side effect of chemotherapy and systemic therapy, involving the loss of hair from the scalp or other body parts. It is caused by the drug's impact on rapidly dividing cells, particularly hair follicles, which can lead to the destruction of healthy cells and result in hair loss. This side effect occurs during treatment and can affect both scalp and body hair. Hair loss is specifically associated with chemotherapy regimens used in the treatment of various conditions, including anal cancer. It is a well-documented potential side effect of chemotherapy, often occurring as a result of damage to hair follicles. The phenomenon is widely recognized as a common consequence of these treatments, affecting patients during their course of therapy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c35816f05289661283f683145d9f395f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
