    <node id="Blood Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Blood Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Blood cancer refers to cancers that originate in the blood or bone marrow, such as acute lymphoblastic leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood cancer is a general term for cancers that affect the blood, bone marrow, and lymphatic system.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood cancer refers to a group of cancers that affect blood cells, including leukemia.&lt;SEP&gt;Blood cancer refers to cancers that affect the blood, bone marrow, or lymphatic system, such as lymphoma and leukemia.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0786666c65b5bf00705439d5cb60d5a0</data>
