    <node id="Immunophenotype">
      <data key="d0">Immunophenotype</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Immunophenotype refers to the specific characteristics of leukemia cells, including the type of lymphocyte and how mature the cells are.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunophenotype refers to the characteristics of leukemia cells, such as the type of lymphocyte involved.&lt;SEP&gt;Immunophenotype refers to the pattern of proteins on the surface of cells, used to identify cell types.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c7205fc2067a4d00e43fd22276db22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648</data>
