      <data key="d5">1772839810</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Supraclavicular Nodes">
      <data key="d0">Supraclavicular Nodes</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Supraclavicular nodes are lymph nodes located above the clavicle.&lt;SEP&gt;Supraclavicular nodes are located above the collarbone and can be affected by breast cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839810</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="G1">
      <data key="d0">G1</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">G1 is a low-grade classification for cancer, indicating less aggressive cell characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;G1 indicates a low-grade tumor with a lower risk of recurrence.&lt;SEP&gt;G1 refers to well-differentiated (low-grade) cancer cells that look like normal cells.&lt;SEP&gt;G1 indicates a low-grade cancer with less abnormal cells.&lt;SEP&gt;G1 refers to low-grade perianal cancer, which is considered for local excision if the surgical margin is free of cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839810</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="G2">
      <data key="d0">G2</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">G2 is an intermediate-grade classification for cancer, indicating moderate aggressiveness.&lt;SEP&gt;G2 indicates a moderate-grade tumor with an intermediate risk of recurrence.&lt;SEP&gt;G2 refers to moderately differentiated (high-grade) cancer cells.&lt;SEP&gt;G2 indicates a moderate-grade cancer with more abnormal cells than G1 but less than G3.&lt;SEP&gt;G2 refers to moderately differentiated (intermediate grade) perianal cancer, which may be considered for local excision under certain conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839810</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="G3">
      <data key="d0">G3</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">G3 is a high-grade classification for cancer, indicating more aggressive cell characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;G3 indicates a high-grade tumor with a higher risk of recurrence.&lt;SEP&gt;G3 refers to poorly differentiated (high-grade) cancer cells that look very different from normal cells.&lt;SEP&gt;G3 indicates a high-grade cancer with highly abnormal cells that grow and spread rapidly.&lt;SEP&gt;G3 refers to poorly differentiated (high-grade) perianal cancer, which typically requires more aggressive treatment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29b3a349650a8bb55b318dcc6ecb0519</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839810</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="GX">
      <data key="d0">GX</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">GX indicates that the grade of cancer cannot be determined.&lt;SEP&gt;GX indicates that the tumor grade cannot be determined.&lt;SEP&gt;GX indicates that the cancer grade cannot be determined.&lt;SEP&gt;GX indicates the grade cannot be determined.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74f18dd51a0091fc888512458a85b0a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839810</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Numbered Stages">
      <data key="d0">Numbered Stages</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Numbered stages are a system used to classify the extent of cancer based on TNM scores and receptor status.&lt;SEP&gt;Numbered stages range from stage 1 to stage 4, with stage 4 being the most advanced.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84367cc8f7a94b97b4b66a1ca127c15f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f05c8ea6f7c7b4ba1fb0ff1c1733980</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839810</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ductal Carcinoma In Situ">
      <data key="d0">Ductal Carcinoma In Situ</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Ductal carcinoma in situ (DCIS) is a noninvasive form of breast cancer found in the milk ducts that has not spread beyond the ducts.&lt;SEP&gt;Ductal Carcinoma In Situ (DCIS) is a noninvasive form of breast cancer found only in the milk ducts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7390896141393e0b4d1c15df77b5c0a7</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839810</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Regional Lymph Nodes">
      <data key="d0">Regional Lymph Nodes</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">Regional lymph nodes are lymph nodes near the breast that may be affected by breast cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Regional lymph nodes are located near the tumor in the breast and are commonly affected by breast cancer spread.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d388da75afb5ea2d01c97e55cb2b872</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839810</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pathology Report">
      <data key="d0">Pathology Report</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A pathology report is a document containing the findings of a pathologist after examining tissue samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Pathology Report is a document that contains the results of a biopsy analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A pathology report is a document that provides detailed information about a cancer diagnosis, including test results and classifications.&lt;SEP&gt;A pathology report is a document containing the findings of a laboratory analysis of tissue or cells.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb41559e96b71d2bb4ea207c806e8d5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-717174ace5855cc823d51c46c9a70648&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f9fe20fe42489996573eb1b436128b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1130b0f6bbe935ceddbafc6ce2740f</data>
