    <node id="Brain Function">
      <data key="d0">Brain Function</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Brain function refers to the abilities of the brain to process information, control body functions, and regulate behavior.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Glial Cells">
      <data key="d0">Glial Cells</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Glial cells are supportive cells in the brain and spinal cord that can develop into gliomas when they grow abnormally.&lt;SEP&gt;Glial cells are supportive cells in the central nervous system that provide structural and functional support to neurons.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bfe00946dcdff3a8a6fb3d73ce6e1</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Glioblastoma">
      <data key="d0">Glioblastoma</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Glioblastoma is a highly aggressive type of glioma that develops from glial cells.&lt;SEP&gt;A glioblastoma is a type of Grade 4 glioma that is the most common and most aggressive form of brain cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc89a92e9a97781ebca0db50abc34939</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nausea and Vomiting">
      <data key="d0">Nausea and Vomiting</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nausea and vomiting can result from increased pressure on the brain caused by a glioma.&lt;SEP&gt;Nausea and vomiting can be caused by a tumor pressing on the brain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Weakness">
      <data key="d0">Weakness</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Weakness is a symptom of gliomas, often affecting one side of the body or causing balance issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Personality Change">
      <data key="d0">Personality Change</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Personality change is a symptom of gliomas, often indicating brain dysfunction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa5247d6b8c17e58ab315a0d641c7ad3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Throat (Oropharynx)">
      <data key="d0">Throat (Oropharynx)</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The throat, specifically the oropharynx, is the focus of the book, including structures like the soft palate, tonsils, and base of the tongue.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38185832d6395b9952def9a72ecc339d</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839812</data>
