    <node id="Scoping Procedures">
      <data key="d0">Scoping Procedures</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Scoping procedures involve the use of a scope to examine internal body structures, often used in diagnosing throat cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Scoping procedures involve the use of scopes to examine internal body areas, often under anesthesia.&lt;SEP&gt;Scoping procedures involve using a thin, tube-shaped tool called a scope to examine internal body structures and take images or biopsies.</data>
