    <node id="Voice Box">
      <data key="d0">Voice Box</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The voice box, also known as the larynx, is a structure in the throat responsible for producing sound and protecting the airway.&lt;SEP&gt;The voice box, or larynx, is a structure in the throat that contains the vocal cords and allows speech.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839825</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vocal Cords">
      <data key="d0">Vocal Cords</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The vocal cords are two folds of tissue in the voice box that vibrate to produce sound.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839826</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Throat">
      <data key="d0">Throat</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The Throat is the passage leading from the mouth to the windpipe, through which air and food pass.&lt;SEP&gt;Throat is the area containing the voice box and part of the digestive and respiratory systems, and is examined during a physical exam.&lt;SEP&gt;The throat is the part of the body that connects the mouth to the esophagus and is examined during various medical procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;The throat is the part of the body that connects the mouth to the esophagus and larynx.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd06bc83e13e7562ce65d6eee1b6024f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae28e3852f4a9f229250fc19eb39036b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839826</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mouth">
      <data key="d0">Mouth</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Mouth, also known as the oral cavity, is the opening of the digestive and respiratory tracts, located in the head and neck region.&lt;SEP&gt;The mouth is the opening of the digestive and respiratory systems, examined in panoramic dental x-rays.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a84075aaac61b0ad85e5f811fc4f24b</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839826</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Teeth">
      <data key="d0">Teeth</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Teeth are the hard structures in the mouth used for chewing, and can be affected by head and neck cancer and its treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Teeth are part of the oral cavity and can be impacted by head and neck cancer and its treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Teeth are hard structures in the mouth used for chewing and are captured in panoramic dental x-rays.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839826</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Jaw">
      <data key="d0">Jaw</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Jaw is the lower part of the face, and can be affected by head and neck cancer and its treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The jaw is a part of the head and neck region that can be affected by cancer and its treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The jaw is the bone structure that supports the teeth and is included in panoramic dental x-rays.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bdde77ad1be3ee9308db3c7703674b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8639a06098656be20a04fe129660616&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839826</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dentures">
      <data key="d0">Dentures</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Dentures are removable prosthetic devices used to replace missing teeth and are planned using panoramic dental x-rays.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-50531346164ea7c08dd087a868b3cc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ad38c9dc069a8ff8df58c42f00eba23</data>
