      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Folic acid is a vitamin in the blood that is essential for DNA synthesis and cell growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Folic acid (folate) is a nutrient measured in blood tests to assess its levels in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Folic acid, also known as folate, is a nutrient that aids in the production of red and white blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Folic acid, also known as folate, is a B-vitamin important for cell division and the formation of red and white blood cells.&lt;SEP&gt;Folic acid is a nutrient that is often checked in blood tests.</data>
