    <node id="Low Platelets">
      <data key="d0">Low Platelets</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Low platelets is a condition where there are fewer than normal numbers of platelets in the blood, which can occur in CLL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839844</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Low Neutrophils">
      <data key="d0">Low Neutrophils</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Low neutrophils is a condition where there are fewer than normal numbers of neutrophils, a type of white blood cell, which can occur in CLL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-098a64d7118fc8e1eb3e91ba0124258c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839844</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Minimal Residual Disease">
      <data key="d0">Minimal Residual Disease</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Minimal residual disease refers to the presence of a small number of cancer cells after treatment, which is a goal of CLL therapy.</data>
