    <node id="Melanoma">
      <data key="d0">Melanoma</data>
      <data key="d1">condition</data>
      <data key="d2">Melanoma is a less common but more aggressive type of skin cancer compared to squamous and basal cell carcinomas.&lt;SEP&gt;Melanoma is a type of cancer that can show p16 overexpression and is associated with HPV-related changes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fa7c7369d88ae71c842152510867223</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839862</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nonmelanoma Skin Cancers">
      <data key="d0">Nonmelanoma Skin Cancers</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Nonmelanoma skin cancers include basal cell and squamous cell carcinomas, which are less aggressive than melanoma.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839862</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sunlight">
      <data key="d0">Sunlight</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Sunlight is a major risk factor for squamous cell skin cancer due to UV radiation exposure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839862</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Indoor Tanning">
      <data key="d0">Indoor Tanning</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Indoor tanning involves the use of tanning machines and is a significant risk factor for skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839862</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Chronic Wounds">
      <data key="d0">Chronic Wounds</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Chronic wounds, such as ulcers and burns, can lead to the development of squamous cell skin cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f1379433bc205cdec8af2edc77613acb</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839862</data>
