    <node id="Mediastinal Gray Zone Lymphomas">
      <data key="d0">Mediastinal Gray Zone Lymphomas</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
      <data key="d2">Mediastinal gray zone lymphomas are a type of lymphoma characterized by features similar to classical Hodgkin lymphoma and non-Hodgkin PMBL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839863</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="MGZL">
      <data key="d0">MGZL</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
      <data key="d2">MGZL stands for Mediastinal Gray Zone Lymphoma, which has features of both classical Hodgkin lymphoma and non-Hodgkin PMBL.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839863</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Involved-Site Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Involved-Site Radiation Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Involved-site radiation therapy (ISRT) is a treatment option for localized MGZL cases.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839863</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thyroid">
      <data key="d0">Thyroid</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The thyroid is a butterfly-shaped gland located in the neck, responsible for producing hormones that regulate metabolism and other body functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839863</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thyroid Hormones">
      <data key="d0">Thyroid Hormones</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Thyroid hormones, such as thyroxine (T4) and triiodothyronine (T3), are essential for regulating body functions like metabolism and temperature.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839864</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parathyroid Glands">
      <data key="d0">Parathyroid Glands</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">The parathyroid glands are four small glands located on the back of the thyroid that regulate calcium levels in the bloodstream.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839864</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thyroid Nodules">
      <data key="d0">Thyroid Nodules</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
      <data key="d2">Thyroid nodules are abnormal growths within the thyroid gland, most of which are benign and often discovered incidentally.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839864</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TSH Test">
      <data key="d0">TSH Test</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The TSH test measures the level of thyroid-stimulating hormone in the blood, helping assess thyroid function.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839864</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Cowden Syndrome">
      <data key="d0">Cowden Syndrome</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
      <data key="d2">Cowden syndrome is an inherited condition associated with an increased risk of thyroid cancer and other health issues.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839864</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Non-Hodgkin PMBL">
      <data key="d0">Non-Hodgkin PMBL</data>
      <data key="d1">disease</data>
      <data key="d2">Non-Hodgkin PMBL is a type of lymphoma that shares features with Mediastinal Gray Zone Lymphoma (MGZL).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-18b5e32980f3efa0cd012e2abab9b9fc</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839864</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ultrasound Probe">
      <data key="d0">Ultrasound Probe</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An ultrasound probe is a device that uses sound waves to create images of internal body structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839864</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Germline Mutation">
      <data key="d0">Germline Mutation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A germline mutation is a genetic change present in all cells of the body, inherited from parents.&lt;SEP&gt;A germline mutation is a type of hereditary mutation that occurs in reproductive cells and can be passed to offspring.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b3c0f6d26f2f58ca13201c1a90b0a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-965e5a6bad03f2129a98be4373f99176</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839864</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Transperineal Biopsy">
      <data key="d0">Transperineal Biopsy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A transperineal biopsy is a procedure where a needle is inserted through the perineum into the prostate to collect tissue samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A transperineal biopsy is a type of prostate biopsy where a needle is inserted through the perineum into the prostate.</data>
