      <data key="d0">Head and Body Aches</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Head and body aches are common side effects of systemic therapy, causing discomfort in various parts of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lung and Breathing Problems">
      <data key="d0">Lung and Breathing Problems</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Lung and breathing problems are severe side effects of systemic therapy, including cough, shortness of breath, and chest pain.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Organ Damage">
      <data key="d0">Organ Damage</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Organ damage is a severe side effect of systemic therapy, affecting major organs such as the liver and kidneys.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rashes">
      <data key="d0">Rashes</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Rashes are a common side effect of systemic therapy, involving skin irritation or inflammation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Skin Problems">
      <data key="d0">Skin Problems</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Skin problems are a common side effect of systemic therapy, involving changes in skin condition or appearance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="QT Interval">
      <data key="d0">QT Interval</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The QT interval is a measure of the time between the start of the Q wave and the end of the T wave in an electrocardiogram.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Spinal Tap">
      <data key="d0">Spinal Tap</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Spinal tap is another term for a lumbar puncture, a procedure that involves inserting a needle into the lower back to collect spinal fluid.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839892</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Thyroid Surgery">
      <data key="d0">Thyroid Surgery</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Thyroid surgery refers to the removal of part or all of the thyroid gland, often performed to treat thyroid cancer or other thyroid conditions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NIFTP">
      <data key="d0">NIFTP</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">NIFTP stands for Noninvasive Follicular Thyroid Neoplasm with Papillary-like Nuclear Features, a type of low-risk thyroid tumor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Follicular Thyroid Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Follicular Thyroid Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Follicular thyroid carcinoma is a type of thyroid cancer that arises from the follicular cells of the thyroid gland.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hürthle Cell Carcinoma">
      <data key="d0">Hürthle Cell Carcinoma</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Hürthle cell carcinoma is another name for oncocytic carcinoma, a rare and aggressive form of thyroid cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fine Needle Aspiration">
      <data key="d0">Fine Needle Aspiration</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Fine needle aspiration is a diagnostic procedure used to collect cells from a lump or mass for examination under a microscope.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Follow-up Care">
      <data key="d0">Follow-up Care</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Follow-up care refers to ongoing medical monitoring and testing after treatment to detect any signs of cancer recurrence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Whole-Body RAI Imaging">
      <data key="d0">Whole-Body RAI Imaging</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Whole-body RAI imaging is a diagnostic test that uses radioactive iodine to detect cancer cells throughout the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Case-by-Case Basis">
      <data key="d0">Case-by-Case Basis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A case-by-case basis refers to individualized medical decisions based on specific patient circumstances and diagnostic findings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lifelong Thyroid Hormone Replacement Therapy">
      <data key="d0">Lifelong Thyroid Hormone Replacement Therapy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Lifelong thyroid hormone replacement therapy is required for patients who have had their thyroid gland completely removed.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Watch-and-Wait Approach">
      <data key="d0">Watch-and-Wait Approach</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The watch-and-wait approach is a strategy of monitoring cancer without immediate treatment, used in some cases of less aggressive thyroid tumors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Stage 2 Ovarian Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Stage 2 Ovarian Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">condition</data>
      <data key="d2">Stage 2 ovarian cancer refers to cancer that has spread beyond the ovaries but not to distant parts of the body.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772839893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Homologous Recombination Deficiency">
      <data key="d0">Homologous Recombination Deficiency</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Homologous recombination deficiency (HRD) is a genetic condition that affects DNA repair mechanisms and influences treatment choices.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c622c677deca24391324ecd5f16ce4a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b44f0b4da13a804cd1dfb917ac7e981</data>
