    <edge source="Chemotherapy" target="Systemic Therapy">
      <data key="d7">13.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Systemic Therapy is a broad category of treatment that includes chemotherapy as one of its key components. Chemotherapy is a type of systemic therapy that uses drugs to kill fast-growing cancer cells, and it is administered intravenously in many cases. This form of treatment is designed to target cancer cells throughout the body, distinguishing it from localized treatments such as intravesical chemotherapy. Systemic therapy encompasses various approaches, with chemotherapy being one of the primary methods used to treat cancers like AML and other types of cancer. The goal of chemotherapy, as a form of systemic therapy, is to destroy or control the growth of cancer cells by targeting their ability to divide and multiply. It is often used as a whole-body treatment, making it effective for cancers that have spread beyond their original site. While the descriptions vary slightly in wording, they all consistently identify chemotherapy as a subset of systemic therapy, emphasizing its role in treating cancer through systemic drug administration.</data>
      <data key="d9">cancer therapy,drug administration,drug-based therapy,therapeutic approach,therapy type,treatment,treatment approach,treatment category,treatment method,treatment modality,treatment type,type,whole-body effect</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-e90bcd28496f1f39a21973656e3e496f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9cc65c1c26b9e24bfb2c8c966f734a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0a584e54ffa22e1c25f839302bcd727&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e45947107c74d8a06e350be57a94a408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9040f5949ae0ff36ce88faa1f4b67ead&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
