    <edge source="Systemic Therapy" target="Targeted Therapy">
      <data key="d7">8.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Systemic Therapy, Targeted Therapy is a classification of cancer treatments that involves the administration of drugs throughout the body to affect cancer cells. Systemic therapy includes targeted therapy, which focuses on specific receptors on cancer cells. Targeted therapy is a subset of systemic therapy that focuses on specific molecular targets, often proteins or genes that are involved in the growth and survival of cancer cells. It is also described as another form of systemic therapy that targets specific cancer features, such as molecules that are unique to cancer cells. This type of therapy is used in the treatment of various cancers, including AML, where it specifically targets cancer-related molecules. Targeted therapy is a type of systemic therapy that focuses on specific molecular targets, and it is considered a form of systemic therapy that specifically targets cancer-related molecules. Overall, targeted therapy represents a specialized approach within the broader category of systemic therapy, designed to interfere with specific aspects of cancer cell function.</data>
      <data key="d9">precision medicine,therapy type,treatment,treatment approach,treatment category,treatment method,treatment modality,type</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-8333423c91919d7adde114b8286cca7e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64895edc4d35c98b293c555e32022a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a158766f46bf752d6cdfe95c92f14547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2be7a2ce722f07b19c80e6e1690a8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6fd03791661f76f6c1a246b2074b2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29c9b8b5fd2cd967c48522af79a9598f</data>
      <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d12">1772839949</data>
      <data key="d13" />
    </edge>
