    <edge source="Nicotine Withdrawal" target="Smoking">
      <data key="d7">3.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Nicotine withdrawal is a physiological response experienced when quitting smoking.&lt;SEP&gt;Nicotine withdrawal is a major obstacle for individuals trying to quit smoking.&lt;SEP&gt;Smoking cessation can lead to nicotine withdrawal as the body adjusts to reduced nicotine intake.</data>
      <data key="d9">addiction management,addictive behavior,cessation difficulty,physiological challenge,physiological response</data>
      <data key="d10">chunk-be6e1cb2fe11f4d9962741c30d446a69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a890e27eba8c63d10f19b85a72fc14a</data>
