    <edge source="PET Scan" target="Cancer Cells">
      <data key="d7">6.0</data>
      <data key="d8">A PET scan helps identify cancer cells by detecting how they use a substance.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer cells appear brighter on a PET scan because they consume sugar at a faster rate than normal cells.&lt;SEP&gt;PET scans are used to detect cancer cells by showing where they are using sugar from the body.&lt;SEP&gt;PET scans can detect cancer cells by showing areas of increased sugar uptake.&lt;SEP&gt;Cancer cells are visualized as bright spots on PET scans.&lt;SEP&gt;PET scans use radioactive glucose to detect cancer cells, which appear brighter due to increased sugar consumption.</data>
